PVD("solomon_islands_vision_2016-2035",{"docs":["","National Development Strategy 2016"],"s":{"1":[[1,"2","1","National Development Strategy Preparation","the Ministry of Development Planning and Aid Coordination (MDPAC) under the guidance of the NDS National Steering Committee was tasked to prepare the National Development Strategy (NDS) 2016-2035.","Ministry of Development Planning and Aid Coordination (MDPAC)"],[1,"2","6","Medium-Term Development Expenditure Strategy","The NDS includes medium term strategies that will guide the Government's development expenditure programme.",""],[1,"4","23","Managing for Results Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","Managing for Results - M&E Performance Monitoring Framework",""],[1,"4","23","Public Financial Management Act and Roadmap","Improved Budget Processes - PFM Act and Roadmap",""],[1,"4","23","Project Identification and Design Pipeline","Improved Project Identification and Design - Project Pipeline",""],[1,"22","7","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Revision","A national infrastructure investment plan (NIIP) has been prepared and is being revised to highlight such key priority investments over the next 5-10 years.",""],[1,"25","14","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Review and Utilization","Review and use the National Infrastructure Investment Plan, ensuring linkages with national policies and planning processes, the private sector and relevant ministerial and donor stakeholders, helping ensure it provides investment opportunities and employment.",""],[1,"47","9","Public Financial Management-Based Planning and Budget Integration","Improve planning and budget operations based on sound PFM practices as set out in the PFM Road Map such as integration of recurrent and development budgets including donor financed programmes.",""],[1,"49","2","Results-Based Implementation and Performance Monitoring","Effective implementation of the NDS requires actions in four main areas: (i) managing for results (performance monitoring - Appendix 2);",""],[1,"49","2","Public Financial Management and Budget Alignment Reform","(ii) improved budget processes to improve effectiveness of expenditure, strengthening the links between NDS, development budget and recurrent budgets (PFM Act and Roadmap - Appendix 3);",""],[1,"49","2","Project Identification and Pipeline Development","(iv) improved project identification and design and development of a pipeline of soundly prepared projects for inclusion in the MTDP to help meet NDS objectives and targets.",""],[1,"49","3","Programme and Project Performance Monitoring Framework","Performance monitoring of programme and project implementation will be improved at both ministerial level and through the central agencies including Ministry of Development Planning and Aid Coordination (MDPAC) and Ministry of Finance and Treasury (MOFT).","Ministry of Development Planning and Aid Coordination (MDPAC) | Ministry of Finance and Treasury (MOFT)"],[1,"49","4","National Development Strategy Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The M&E Framework sets out performance indicators both at the strategic NDS level, showing alignment with the SDGs, and at the program level.","line ministries | MDPAC"],[1,"49","5","Performance Monitoring Framework Operational Plan","An operational plan for the Performance Monitoring Framework will be developed reconfirming data sources, collection and reporting methodologies and establishing baselines where they do not exist.",""],[1,"49","6","Public Financial Management Reform Framework","The Public Financial Management Act of 2013 became effective in January 2014 and proposes a series of major reforms in Solomon Islands' public financial management, providing a framework for sound financial management and enhancing transparency and accountability in the use of public resources.",""],[1,"49","6","Multi-year Budget Projection and Budget Integration Reform","The framework includes reforms designed to strengthen multi-year budget projections, integrate the recurrent and development budgets, and strengthen the alignment and reporting of donor partners' development assistance.",""],[1,"50","1","Term Development Plan for Financial Decision-Making Coordination","Term Development Plan designed to improve effectivity and coordination of the government's financial decision making processes.",""],[1,"50","2","Medium-Term Development Plan as Central Planning Document","The Roadmap intends the MTDP to become SIG's central multi-year planning document.",""],[1,"50","2","Annual Parliamentary Tabling Requirement for the MTDP","The Act requires that the MTDP be tabled in Parliament before the end of September each year.",""],[1,"50","2","Coordination of Development and Fiscal Planning","The Roadmap aims for coordination of the MTDP and fiscal and budget strategies, which should be \"published at the same time\".",""],[1,"50","2","Strengthening Links Between Development Plans, Corporate Plans, Sector Policies, and the Budget","The Roadmap intends to strengthen the links between the MTDP and corporate plans and sector policies as well as the budget.",""],[1,"50","2","Medium-Term Budget Framework Introduction","Preparation of a medium term budget framework is under consideration and will be introduced.",""],[1,"51","4","Expanded NIIP Project Pipeline Development","It is intended that the NIIP, with an expanded sector coverage, be used as a pipeline of projects for inclusion in the NDS and future MTDPs.",""],[1,"51","4","Early Submission and NIIP Appraisal Process","New project ideas should be submitted as early as possible to MDPAC and undergo the rigorous analytical approach of the NIIP.","MDPAC"],[1,"51","4","Future Project Funding Pipeline Development","In this way the government can develop a pipeline of projects ready for future funding.",""],[1,"54","24","Public Financial Management and Output Budgeting Reform","economic management - (i) improved financial mgmt. and reporting; (ii) medium term budget framework: (iii) moves to output budgeting",""],[1,"69","30","Public Financial Management Planning and Budget Operations Improvement","Improve planning and budget operations in line with the PFM Road Map",""],[1,"72","2","Medium-Term Development Plan as Central Planning Document","The Roadmap intends the MTDP to become the Government's central multi-year planning document.",""],[1,"72","2","Annual Tabling of the Medium-Term Development Plan in Parliament","The Act requires that the MTDP be tabled in Parliament before the end of September each year.",""],[1,"72","2","Coordination of Development, Fiscal, and Budget Strategies","The Roadmap aims for coordination of the MTDP, fiscal and budget strategies, which should be \"published at the same time\".",""],[1,"72","2","Alignment of MTDP with Corporate Plans, Sector Policies, and Budget Frameworks","The Roadmap intends to strengthen the links between the MTDP and corporate plans and sector policies as well as the budget and medium term budget framework (MTBF) documents.",""],[1,"72","4","Improved Budget Consultation and Coordination Mechanism","Item 3.4.03 proposes greater consultation and coordination between MDPAC and MOFT in budget preparation, continuing the developments already begun.","MDPAC | MOFT"],[1,"72","6","Training and Simplified Appraisal Template Development","much more training is required to achieve this and simplified templates need to be developed.",""],[1,"73","1","Integration of Planning and Budget Processes","The MTDP process has focused on linking planning and budget processes.",""],[1,"73","1","Coordination of MTDP and MDPAC with Corporate and Sectoral Planning","it is necessary that the MTDP and MDPAC planning also be closely involved with the corporate and sectoral planning processes, as proposed in item 3.4.10 in the Roadmap.",""],[1,"73","2","Medium-Term Development Plan as Link Between Multi-Year Plans and Annual Budget Process","The MTDP, therefore, needs to be a link between multi-year plans and annual budget process in order to strengthen multi-year budget projections and support development of the MTBF, as intended at 3.4.11.",""],[1,"73","4","Regulatory Framework for Multi-Year Planning and Budgeting","Multi-year planning and budgeting require complete data on a proposal and the rejection of proposals with incomplete information, appropriately supported by regulations.",""],[1,"74","1","Budget Coordination Committee for Joint Budget Consultations","This process has been strengthened through the creation of a Budget Coordination Committee (BCC) that also includes representatives from the MPS and the OPMC.",""],[1,"74","5","Medium-Term Development Plan Tabling Requirement","Table in Parliament the MTDP at least 3 months before the start of the financial year (PFM Act S45 (2) which need to be consistent to the budget and fiscal strategies.",""],[1,"74","6","Regulatory Framework for MTDP Implementation","Develop regulations to support the MTDP and its implementation (PFM Act S45 (2)).",""],[1,"74","9","Budget Process Review and Coordination Reform","Review budget process on both recurrent and development budget to strengthen coordination and promote greater integration (PEFA).",""],[1,"74","10","Inclusion of Project Recurrent Costs in the Recurrent Budget","Include recurrent costs of projects in recurrent budget (PEFA).",""],[1,"74","11","Incorporate Development Expenditure Strategy into Budget Strategy Paper","Include development expenditure strategy in the budget strategy paper.",""],[1,"74","13","Integration of Development Budget into Midyear Budget Review","Make the development budget an integral part of midyear budget review to enable MDPAC to assess and discuss with LMs the rate of implementation of the development budget.",""],[1,"74","14","Budget Reconciliation and Project Proposal Capacity Assessment","Reconcile differences between the development budget and recurrent budget (PEFA): · Payment of wages and salaries of program staff. · Require project proposals to the tender boards and Cabinet to include assessment of the capacity of LMs to",""],[1,"75","4","Align Development Expenditure with Local Government Implementation Capacity","Better match allocation of development expenditure to implementation capacity of LMs.",""],[1,"75","5","Funding Access Facilitation at MOFT","Facilitate access to funding at MOFT during the year.","MOFT"],[1,"75","7","Adopt MTDP as Main Development Budget Planning Instrument","Adopt MTDP as the main planning instrument for development budget:",""],[1,"75","8","Annual MTDP Update Mechanism","Update MTDP yearly to carry forward those not funded in particular year.",""],[1,"75","9","Training for Local Managers on Development and Recurrent Budgets","Undertake training of LMs on the link between development and recurrent budgets.",""],[1,"75","9","Clarification of the MTDP-MTEF Linkage","Clarify the link between MTDP and MTEF.",""],[1,"75","10","Multiyear Development Planning Improvement through MTEF-MTDP Linkages","Improve multiyear development planning through the MTEF (PEFA) and the linkages between MTEF and MTDP.",""],[1,"75","11","Development Budget and Budget Process Awareness Programme","Undertake awareness program to improve the understanding of the importance of development budget in the economy and the budget processes (integrate with the Roadmap awareness and ownership programme).",""],[1,"75","14","Parliamentary Appropriation Alignment for Donor Funding","Progressively reduce donor funding that are not appropriated by Parliament: 1. Improve the accuracy of forward estimates 2. Align forward estimates with the requirement of the PFM Act and definition of public funds",""],[1,"76","11","National Development Strategy and Medium-Term Development Planning Framework","SIG will produce, in a consultative and transparent manner involving all stakeholders, a twenty-year National Development Strategy (2016-35), a Medium Term Development Plan (2016-2020) as well as associated Sector or Ministry Corporate Plans that set out the Government's development priorities.",""],[1,"76","13","Parliamentary Reporting for Transparency and Accountability","SIG will follow existing policies and processes in reporting to Parliament and associated statutory authorities to promote transparency and accountability in the identification of national priorities and in the budget and implementation decisions that ensure all development resources (SIG and external) are used to promote inclusive sustainable development for all Solomon Islanders).",""],[1,"77","3","Public Finance Management Reform Roadmap Implementation","SIG will implement the reforms outlined in Public Finance Management Reform Roadmap.",""]],"3":[[1,"48","1","Decentralization and Federal Governance Review","Inclusive stable governance - encourage decentralization of decision making in the country and examine Federal system of government.",""],[1,"48","2","Strengthen Provincial and National Planning Ownership","Improve the focus and ownership of provincial and national plans by recognising the diversity of provinces and their different challenges and opportunities.",""],[1,"48","3","National-Provincial Government and Resource Owner Coordination","Strengthen communications and cooperation between national and provincial governments and resource owners.",""],[1,"48","4","Community Partnership for Policy Implementation","Active partnership with local institutions and rural communities, such as civic groups, church and chiefs in implementing government policies.",""],[1,"48","9","Political Party Integrity Act Review","Political stability - review of Political Party Integrity Act, \"Electoral (Provision) Ac\", implementation of Constitutional reform programmes and Federal System of Government in the country.",""],[1,"48","9","Electoral Provision Act Review","Political stability - review of Political Party Integrity Act, \"Electoral (Provision) Ac\", implementation of Constitutional reform programmes and Federal System of Government in the country.",""],[1,"48","9","Constitutional Reform Programme","Political stability - review of Political Party Integrity Act, \"Electoral (Provision) Ac\", implementation of Constitutional reform programmes and Federal System of Government in the country.",""],[1,"48","9","Federal System of Government Implementation","Political stability - review of Political Party Integrity Act, \"Electoral (Provision) Ac\", implementation of Constitutional reform programmes and Federal System of Government in the country.",""]],"4":[[1,"11","10","Governance, Accountability, and Anti-Corruption Strengthening","Good governance values and practices need to be enforced and accountability and transparency enhanced at all levels of governance.",""],[1,"11","10","National Unity Strengthening Initiative","National unity needs to be strengthened through shared visions and agreed social and economic development goals.",""],[1,"14","5","Governance, Accountability, and Transparency Strengthening","Good governance values and practices need to be enforced and accountability and transparency enhanced at all levels of governance.",""],[1,"14","5","Public Service Corporate Culture Reform","A sound corporate culture needs to be embedded in the public service.",""],[1,"14","5","Anti-Corruption Eradication Initiative","Corruption needs to be eradicated, both within and outside the public service.",""],[1,"14","5","National Unity and Shared Vision Initiative","National unity needs to be strengthened through shared visions and agreed social and economic development goals.",""],[1,"14","5","Law and Order Maintenance","Law and order need to be maintained to provide stability.",""],[1,"46","6","Anti-Corruption and Governance Improvement Strategy","Medium Term Strategy 13: Reduce Corruption and improve governance at national, provincial and community levels: The objective of this strategy is to reduce corruption within government institutions and to instil a sound corporate culture at all levels",""],[1,"47","16","Anti-Corruption and Good Governance Promotion","Increase efforts focused on preventing corruption and mal- practice and create a good governance culture.",""],[1,"47","17","Anti-Corruption Legal and Institutional Reform","Review and strengthen anti-corruption legislation and related subsidiary legislations based on national consensus regarding the laws and mechanisms that must be established and implemented at national and provincial levels to combat corruptions including the Establishment of the Solomon Islands Independent Commission against corruption (SIICAC) in compliance with international anti-corruption conventions and initiatives.",""],[1,"47","18","Support for Oversight Institutions and Civic Organizations","Support and empower watch-dog institutions to provide necessary oversight to public institutions and support programmes to civic organisations.",""],[1,"69","19","Public Access to Information and Fundamental Freedoms Protection","Ensure public access to information and protect fundamental freedoms, in accordance with national legislation and international agreements.",""],[1,"70","11","Publication of Payments Under Resource Contracts","Publication of all payments made to governments under resource contracts.",""],[1,"70","12","Anti-Corruption Legislation","Prevention of corruption and mal-practice - anti-corruption legislation",""]],"5":[[1,"18","3","Mining Regulation Development and Enforcement","there is a need to develop and enforce mining regulations",""],[1,"20","2","Mining Act Review and Enforcement","Review and enforce the Mining Act in collaboration with various stakeholders, including landowners to improve sustainable mining resource management.",""],[1,"20","3","Mineral Resource Governance and Licensing Framework","Introduce and facilitate environmental and economic assessments, licensing agreements, accountability laws and policies between potential investors, landowners, concerned communities and government on exploitation of the mineral resources.",""],[1,"29","1","Coordination on Mineral and Hydrocarbon Resource Development","between government, provinces and resource owners on prospective developments in their areas in order to facilitate exploration and exploitation of mineral and hydrocarbon resources.",""],[1,"29","2","Mineral Investment Licensing and Compliance Framework","Facilitate exploitation of mineral prospects by guiding investors to conclude lease agreements, social studies, environmental impact assessments, rehabilitation and mining agreements and issue licenses only after such requirements have been fulfilled.",""],[1,"55","17","Mining Sector Export Earnings Expansion","Increase GDP contribution in mining sector through export earnings.",""]],"6":[[1,"12","3","Economic Growth Centres Development","A key strategy is to develop economic growth centres and rural growth centres.",""],[1,"12","4","Productive Sector Reinvigoration Programme","The productive and resource sectors (agriculture, livestock, agro-forestry, aquaculture, marine resources and fisheries including small scale rural fisheries, tourism, forestry and reforestation, mining and energy) need reinvigorating to increase value added and export earnings and to achieve sustained growth.",""],[1,"15","2","Economic Growth Centres Development","A key strategy is to develop economic growth centres and rural growth centres.",""],[1,"15","2","Productive and Resource Sector Revitalization","The productive and resource sectors need reinvigorating to increase value added and export earnings and to achieve sustained growth.",""],[1,"15","2","Agriculture, Fisheries, Forestry, Minerals and Tourism Development","Development of agriculture, fisheries, forestry, minerals and tourism are all important.",""],[1,"18","16","Natural Resource Base Development for Growth and Employment","Improve growth, employment and manufacturing prospects through development of the natural resource base.",""],[1,"19","2","Natural Resource Commercialization and Downstream Processing Promotion","Improve the balance of payments through the commercialization of natural resources and promotion of downstream processing.",""],[1,"20","6","Foreign Investment and Trade Policy Clarification","Foreign investment and trade policy needs to be clear, with care taken over any investment protection policies and treaties.",""],[1,"20","9","Integrated Trade Policy and Development Planning","Trade policy and development need to be planned, implemented and managed in an integrated way.",""],[1,"22","3","National Trade Policy Implementation","Implement the National Trade Policy as a key element in economic growth, encouraging sustainable trade and investment.",""],[1,"22","4","National Trade Agreement Consultation Process","Conduct national consultations with all relevant stakeholders on multilateral, regional and bi-lateral trade agreements including PACP-EU Economic Partnership Agreement, PACER Plus, PICTA, MSGTA, ensuring better alignment to identified trade, economic and development interests of Solomon Islands.",""],[1,"22","5","Trade Coordination with Diplomatic Missions","Increase coordination with SI Diplomatic Missions on trade- related issues and liaise with Missions and trade related technical assistance from multilateral, regional and bilateral agencies.",""],[1,"22","6","Strengthening of the National Trade Development Council","Strengthen the National Trade Development Council (NTDC) to coordinate trade related issues including trade mainstreaming, needs assessments and consensus building on trade negotiations.",""],[1,"31","1","Local Food Production and Downstream Processing Programmes","Prepare programmes and projects that promote local food production and where possible develop downstream processing for value adding to local and overseas markets.",""]],"7":[[1,"19","10","Community Fisheries Development Support","Promote artisanal and semi commercial activities by providing incentives, market access and relevant supporting infrastructure to foster community fisheries development; diversify and introduce appropriate aquaculture systems.",""]],"8":[[1,"43","4","Agricultural Disaster Risk Management and Climate Change Mitigation","farmers shielded from impacts of natural disasters and climate change through disaster and risk management and climate change mitigation","Ministry of Agriculture and livestock"],[1,"43","4","Soil Conservation and Land Productivity Improvement","soil conservation and management enhanced, land fertility and productivity increased, land use planning and policies in place","Ministry of Agriculture and livestock"],[1,"43","4","Agricultural Regulatory Framework Enforcement","appropriate regulatory framework in place and enforced","Ministry of Agriculture and livestock"],[1,"45","2","Environmentally Sound Subsistence Farming Development","Promote development of environmentally sound and sustainable subsistence based farming systems including organic farming, indigenous crops, and improved post-harvest handling, increased household food security and marketable surpluses and downstream processing.",""],[1,"45","3","Integrated Agriculture and Land Management for Agro-ecosystem Conservation","Support conservation and sustainable use of natural resources for food security and agriculture through integrated agriculture and land management strategies and the conservation and rehabilitation of agro-ecosystems.",""],[1,"45","4","Vulnerability and Adaptation Assessment Programme","Undertake province and nation-wide vulnerability and adaptation assessments and determine most vulnerable communities or sectors and identify relevant adaptation technology options in order to improve their resilience to climate change impacts.",""],[1,"45","11","Climate Change Adaptation Measures for Food Production","Collaborate with development partners to identify possible impacts of climate change of food production and security and identify measures to mitigate/adapt to the impacts of climate change on food production.",""],[1,"60","12","Sustainable Food Production and Resilient Agriculture Programme","By 2030, ensure sustainable food production systems and implement resilient agricultural practices that increase productivity and production, that help maintain ecosystems, that strengthen capacity for adaptation to climate change, extreme weather, drought, flooding and other disasters and that progressively improve land and soil quality.",""]],"9":[[1,"18","2","Reforestation and Plantation Development","More emphasis is needed on reforestation and plantation development and on downstream processing and value adding.",""],[1,"18","2","Review of Forestry Regulatory Compliance Framework","The regulatory environment particularly compliance needs to be reviewed.",""],[1,"18","2","Private Sector Forestry Development and Marketing Partnership","Private sector involvement in forestry is critically important for developing, managing, and conserving forest resources as well as for processing and marketing of forest products.",""],[1,"18","2","Public-Private Financing for Sustainable Forest Management","Public-private partnerships could bring innovative financing mechanisms for sustainable forest management through re-forestation and are promising.",""],[1,"19","14","Local Forestry Replanting and Non-Timber Forest Processing Policy","Establish policies that encourage replanting of local forestry species, downstream processing of forestry resources and other non-timber resources such as medicinal herbs and mushrooms.",""],[1,"19","15","Forestry Law Amendment and Update for Plantation Promotion","Amend or update forestry laws to assist land owning groups including farmers to promote establishment of forest plantations including reforestation and promotion of sustainable harvesting.",""],[1,"19","16","Agro-forestry Scheme Support and Promotion","Support and promote agro-forestry schemes through promotion of improved methods, research and improved marketing and supporting infrastructure and facilities.",""],[1,"29","4","Holistic Forest Management and Logging Control","Protect natural resources, environment and conservation and strive to adopt a holistic management approach for the country's forests by properly controlling the activities of the logging industry to achieve a better balance in the pecuniary and social benefits received by government and resource owners.",""],[1,"29","5","Forest Conservation, Reforestation, and Sustainable Logging Reform","Protect remaining forest resources and re-establish forests, sustainably manage logging extractions in the remaining forests, including through increased taxation and emphasize reforestation to replace the depleted forest cover, with MFR leading a review of Forestry Acts in close consultation with provinces and resource owners.","MFR"]],"10":[[1,"12","9","Weather-Resilient Infrastructure and Utilities Upgrade","Medium Term Strategy 3: Expand and upgrade weather resilient infrastructure and utilities focused on access to productive resources and markets and to essential services",""],[1,"25","8","Renewable Energy Development Programme","Develop renewable energy resources including Tina River and Fiu River hydropower schemes.",""],[1,"25","13","Weather-Resilient Infrastructure and Utilities Upgrade","MTS 3: Expand and upgrade weather resilient infrastructure and utilities focused on access to productive resources and markets and to essential services.",""],[1,"27","5","Integrated Energy Sector Planning and Policy Implementation","Strengthen energy sector planning and policy implementation through an integrated approach supported by appropriate capacity and dissemination of energy related information through school curricula, community training and wider consultations on policy issues, legislation and regulations.",""],[1,"27","6","Urban Power Supply Reliability and Affordability Reform","Ensure reliable and affordable power supply in all urban centres by promoting use of renewable energy, opening the market to Independent Power Providers (IPP), appropriate pre-paid tariff structures and ensuring SIEA has sound technical and managerial expertise for an efficient and effective SOE.",""],[1,"27","7","Rural Renewable Electricity Expansion","Increase the supply and coverage of electricity in rural areas using renewable energy resources, focusing on hydro-power in larger islands and solar power on water short atolls and outer islands whilst evaluating other renewable resources and adopting both appropriate technologies and institutional arrangements including community management, PPP and IPP.",""],[1,"27","7","Energy Conservation and Efficiency Measures","Reduce energy costs by promote energy conservation and efficiency, in the context of the introduction of product standards for appliances including appliance labelling, energy efficiency ratings and promotion of energy efficient technology and ensure minimal negative environmental impacts of energy production, distribution and consumption on the environment.",""]],"11":[[1,"24","1","Urban Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement","there is also an urgent need for improvement in water supply and sanitation in Honiara and urban centres.",""],[1,"24","1","Alternative Water Sources and Treatment Development","alternative water sources and treatment is identified and made operational within a few years.",""],[1,"24","1","Urban Sewerage Services Improvement","the ongoing health and environmental effects of improper water and sanitation services needs to be better understood, funded and improvements delivered.",""],[1,"25","7","Water and Sanitation Utilities Improvement and Maintenance","Improve and maintain utilities notably water and sanitation services.",""],[1,"26","16","Solomon Islands Water Authority Reform and Commercial Viability Programme","Foster and enhance continuous reform at Solomon Islands Water Authority (SIWA).",""],[1,"26","17","Urban Water and Sewerage Strategic Plan","Develop a Strategic Plan identifying the needs for urban water and sewerage for the next 25 years especially given the rapid growth of Honiara.",""],[1,"26","18","Urban Sewerage and Sanitation Expansion","Ensure proper sanitation is available in all sewered communities and that environmental effects of sewage disposal are adequately addressed.",""],[1,"27","1","Safe and Sufficient Water Supply Service","Ensure the water provided to all customers is sufficient and chemically safe to appropriate World Health Organisation standards.",""],[1,"27","3","Water Supply and Sanitation System Expansion and Upgrade","Examine need to upgrade and extend coverage of water supply and sanitation systems in urban, peri-urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"27","3","National Water and Sanitation Policy Development","Develop a national policy on the provision of water and sanitation to improve health and service provision in Honiara, Auki and other provincial centres and rural areas.",""],[1,"27","4","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Measures","Improve ongoing strategies and practices to deal with the significant non-revenue water lost through theft and leakage as well as significant debt incurred by many customers.",""],[1,"31","6","Water and Sanitation Availability Initiative","Ensure availability of water and sanitation.",""]],"12":[[1,"27","2","Water Catchment Forest Conservation and Water Source Protection","Preserve and properly manage water catchment forest areas.",""]],"13":[[1,"35","2","NRH Relocation","Immediate priority activities include the relocation of NRH",""],[1,"35","2","Medical Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Construction Programme","other medium term priorities include rehabilitation, reconstruction and construction of new medical infrastructures in rural and urban centres",""],[1,"37","12","Health Knowledge Utilization in Extractive Industries","Ensure previous knowledge, experiences and recommendations of working effectively with health is utilised by all including extractive industries.",""],[1,"37","21","Health Workforce and Referral System Strengthening","Ensure staffing numbers, competencies and motivation are sufficient to provide identified service packages including medical supply distribution, funding for operation and decision making for referral between provinces and facility levels.",""],[1,"37","29","Evidence-Based Health Care Infrastructure Development","Build health care infrastructure based the evidence of its impact",""],[1,"37","30","Primary Health Care Infrastructure and Equipment Rehabilitation","Rehabilitate and strengthen primary health care infrastructure and equipment.",""],[1,"37","31","Relocation of NRH Secondary and Tertiary Functions","Relocate the secondary and tertiary functions of the NRH to a new location is a medium term priority.",""],[1,"38","1","Laboratory Facilities Strengthening Programme","Strengthen programme for laboratory facilities to meet current and future demand.",""],[1,"38","2","Hospital Rehabilitation and Equipment Upgrade Programme","Rehabilitate regional and provincial - secondary and specialty (mental health) hospitals including tertiary infrastructure and equipment.",""]],"14":[[1,"13","8","Universal Secondary Education Access Expansion","The overarching strategic goal is to provide universal access to quality secondary education for all children by 2030 and improved access to technical and vocational education and training and higher education.",""],[1,"13","8","Education Expenditure Refocusing for Primary and Junior Secondary Services","Government will place priority on refocusing education sector expenditure on providing services at primary and junior secondary schools to achieve the target of achieving universal completion of quality junior secondary by 2030.",""],[1,"31","8","Inclusive Education Policy","Establish a policy on inclusive education for all with greater emphasis on free education and ensure its effectiveness in terms of physical and teacher's quality as role model.",""],[1,"38","12","Education Sector Strategy for Universal Secondary Education","The Ministry of Education and Human Resource Development has developed a new education sector strategy.","Ministry of Education and Human Resource Development"],[1,"38","12","Education Expenditure Reallocation to Primary and Junior Secondary Schools","Government will place priority on refocusing education sector expenditure on providing services at primary and junior secondary schools to achieve the target of achieving universal completion of quality junior secondary by 2030.",""],[1,"38","16","Secondary Education Skills Development","Ensure that secondary education delivers both work-related skills and transferable skills, including entrepreneurial and ICT skills to increase the number of youth who have relevant skills for employment, decent jobs and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"39","4","Education Institution Resourcing and Safe Facilities Provision","adequately and equitably resourcing education institutions and programmes with safe and easily-accessible facilities;",""],[1,"39","10","Cross-Sector Equity and Inclusive Education Policy Development","Cross-sector policies and plans will be developed to address the social, cultural and economic barriers that deprive children, youth and adults of education and quality learning.",""],[1,"39","13","Inclusive School Facilities Development","development of inclusive school facilities;",""],[1,"39","14","Teacher Training on Inclusive Education","extend teacher training on inclusive education;",""],[1,"39","15","Vernacular Language Policy Mainstreaming","mainstreaming use of vernacular language policies to address exclusion.",""],[1,"39","16","Gender-Sensitive Education Measures","Further gender-sensitive measures are needed to ensure that teaching and learning have an equal impact on girls and boys and to ensure the personal security of girls in and on the journey to and from education institutions.",""],[1,"39","16","Education Equity Data and Monitoring System","It is also necessary to develop more systematic approaches to collect, analyse, and use disaggregated data to measure marginalization in education and set targets for reducing inequity and to monitor progress towards these targets.",""],[1,"41","16","Equitable Access and Completion Policy for Priority Groups","Design and implement affordable and effective policies to allow equitable access and to improve completion for priority target groups.",""],[1,"41","17","Community Partnership for Basic Education Access and Completion","Work in partnership with communities to improve access and completion in basic education.",""],[1,"41","18","Exclusion Diagnostics Capacity Development","Fully develop the capacity to diagnose the size and leading causes of exclusion for all priority target groups by 2020.",""],[1,"41","19","Introduction of Vernacular Languages in Primary Education","Determine affordable solutions to introduce the use of vernacular languages in primary education by 2018.",""],[1,"41","20","Education System Internal Efficiency Improvement","Improve internal efficiency of the education system.",""],[1,"41","22","Primary and Junior Secondary Education Quality Improvement","Continue improving the quality and relevance of primary and junior secondary education.",""],[1,"41","25","Affordable Senior Secondary Access Expansion Solutions","Determine affordable solutions for expanding access for Senior Secondary.",""],[1,"65","9","Gender Equality in Education and Vocational Training Access","By 2030, eliminate gender disparities in education and ensure equal access to all levels of education and vocational training for the vulnerable, including persons with disabilities, indigenous peoples and children in vulnerable situations [SDG 4.5].",""]],"15":[[1,"12","4","ICT Expansion and Improvement Initiative","Information and communications technology is currently under-prioritised and need expansion and improvement.",""],[1,"25","9","Community Telecommunications Connectivity Initiative","ICT - link communities with telecommunication networks.",""],[1,"25","10","Fiber Optic Submarine Cable and Broadband Services Expansion","Establish fiber optic submarine cable system and provide broad band services.",""],[1,"27","8","ICT Coverage Expansion Initiative","Encourage development and spread of ICT coverage.",""],[1,"58","11","Universal and Affordable Internet Access Expansion","Significantly increase access to information and communications technology and strive to provide universal and affordable access to the Internet in least developed countries by 2020.",""]],"16":[[1,"17","3","Domestic Air Services Expansion Through Aircraft Leasing","The long-term lease of a Dash 8 aircraft has made an important improvement to domestic air services, enabling more flights and higher load factor.",""],[1,"23","7","International Airport Equipment Upgrade and Maintenance","Current programmes focus on: (i) upgrading and maintenance of equipment at the international airport including the replacement of the navigational equipment (DVOR/DME)",""],[1,"23","7","Provincial Airstrip Maintenance and Upgrading","and (ii) maintenance and upgrading of provincial airstrips.",""],[1,"25","5","Airport Rehabilitation and Development Programme","Rehabilitate and develop international and domestic airports throughout Solomon Islands including all weather airstrips.",""],[1,"25","6","Civil Aviation Safety Standards Enforcement","Enforce international civil aviation safety standards.",""],[1,"26","12","Civil Aviation Institutional Separation and Regulatory Strengthening","Enforce the Civil Aviation Act separating policy, regulatory and service provider functions and empowering CAASI to ensure a safe aviation environment and conditions.",""],[1,"26","13","Aviation Weather Services Quality Management System","Establish and implement the Quality Management System for aviation weather services to improve services to domestic and international flights and meet the certification requirements of CAASI and the International Civil Aviation Organisation.",""],[1,"26","14","Airport Operation Outsourcing and Expansion Review","Review outsourcing of service delivery provision in the operation ensure sustainability and provision to expand as required by international aviation laws/ regulation.",""]],"17":[[1,"33","3","Support for Vulnerable and Disadvantaged Groups","Provide support to the vulnerable including women, children and other vulnerable and disadvantaged groups such as the elderly and disabled",""],[1,"33","4","Community Engagement Programmes for Women, Youth and Children","Develop community engagement programmes that address the needs of women, youth and children and which encourage social and communal stability.",""],[1,"33","6","National Youth Policy and Youth Sports Development","Promote the social and communal aspects of the youth development and a national youth policy and link to development of national and provincial sports activities.",""],[1,"33","7","Social and Community Security Policy Improvement","Improve social and communal security including related policies.",""],[1,"33","14","Rural School Attendance and Social Services Improvement Programme","Develop programmes and specific policies that will improve attendance of children in schools in rural areas, and improve the provision of social services to the aged and disabled persons in rural areas.",""],[1,"33","20","Support for Disabled Society and Responsible Bodies","Strengthen support to responsible bodies such as the disabled society to support both disadvantage and advantage groups.",""],[1,"33","21","Rural Support Centres for Vulnerable Groups","Develop policy and programmes for the establishment of support centres for vulnerable, disadvantaged including disabled, women and children and elderly people in rural areas.",""],[1,"59","13","National Social Protection Systems and Measures","Implement nationally appropriate social protection systems and measures for all, including floors, and by 2030 achieve substantial coverage of the poor and the vulnerable",""],[1,"59","19","Special Measures to Increase Development Opportunities for Women, Youth, Children and Families","Special measures to increase development opportunities for women, youth, children and their families are in place by 2020",""]],"18":[[1,"73","8","Comprehensive Aid Coordination Strategy Development and Implementation","First, completing development of a comprehensive aid coordination strategy and then implementing it in partnership with donors.","MDPAC"],[1,"73","8","Sector and Planning Staff Involvement in Programme Preparation","Second, through the involvement of sector and planning staff in the preparation of proposed programmes to optimise their design in relation to SIG objectives and benefits to Solomon Islanders.",""],[1,"75","12","Donor Assistance Alignment and Reporting Mechanism","To strengthen alignment and reporting of donor assistance:",""],[1,"75","13","Donor Assistance Alignment Mechanism","Strengthen alignment of donor assistance to the MTDP through donor policies and SIG strategies.",""],[1,"75","15","Increase Use of National Systems by Development Partners","Increase the use of national systems by development partners as confidence in the development budget management increases (PEFA).",""],[1,"75","16","Multiyear Development Partner Assistance Allocation Requirement","Require development partners to provide multiyear allocation of assistance according to budget classification and to address different financial years of donors (PEFA).",""],[1,"76","1","Partnership Framework for Development Cooperation","The Partnership Framework is a shared declaration of intent between the Government of Solomon Islands and its Development Partners and does not constitute a legally binding document.",""],[1,"76","8","Inclusive Policy and Programme Design Mechanism","SIG will take stronger leadership of its own development policies and will engage with its Parliament, local authorities and citizens in shaping those policies and in the design and implementation of associated programmes and projects.",""],[1,"76","9","Program and Sector-Based Aid Coordination Approach","SIG and Development Partners will work to establish and strengthen program and/or sector based approach rather than a project-based approach.",""],[1,"76","10","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for SIG","SIG strengthens its institutional capacity with support from the development partners.",""],[1,"76","12","Stakeholders Forum Reinvigoration and Development Partner Coordination","SIG will consult with development partners in order to reinvigorate the Stakeholders Forum.",""],[1,"77","2","Development Partner Initiative Design Negotiation Mechanism","SIG will negotiate the design of development initiatives with individual or coalitions of development partners in an open and transparent manner",""],[1,"77","4","Development Partner Dialogue and Coordination Mechanism","SIG will maintain an open dialogue with all development partners, including State-owned enterprises, Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs), Faith-Based Organizations (FBOs), philanthropic organizations, academia and the private sector to ensure comprehensive approach to development effectiveness.",""],[1,"77","5","Aid Flow Recording and Budget Documentation Capacity","SIG will ensure that it has the statistical and information management capacity to record aid flows and to ensure that the funding support of all development partners' is recorded in the budget documents.",""],[1,"77","6","Institutional and Human Resource Capacity Strengthening for Public Sector Systems","SIG will strengthen institutions, systems and processes and build its human resource capacity, and development partners will use the country systems for development assistance supported programs in support of activities managed by the public sector.",""],[1,"77","6","Joint Assessment of Country Systems and Procedures","SIG and development partners will jointly assess quality of country systems and procedures in a country-led process using mutually agreed diagnostic tools.",""],[1,"77","7","Non-State Actor Engagement in Development Policy and Implementation","SIG and Development Partners acknowledge the importance of non-state-actors as key partners in achieving effective aid outcomes and will involve them in the development and implementation of Solomon Islands' development policies and priorities.",""],[1,"77","8","Development Partner Coordination and Capacity Support for SIG Leadership","Development partners will respect SIG leadership and contribute to further strengthening its capacity to exercise it.",""],[1,"77","11","Development Partner Coordination and Simplified Procedures","Development Partners implement arrangements and simplified procedures as identified in the Paris declaration, Accra Agenda for Action and the Busan Partnership commitments.",""],[1,"77","12","Development Partner Policy Dialogue and Aid Coordination Compliance","Development Partners will base their development policy dialogue with Government on the poverty reduction and growth agenda articulated in the MTDP and related national and sectoral plans and in doing so, undertake to respect SIG development cooperation policies and procedures; follow the SIG approval processes for all development assistance; and acknowledge the central coordinating and monitoring role of the MDPAC.",""],[1,"77","13","Development Partner Support for National Systems and Budget Support","Development Partners will support all efforts of the SIG to strengthen their national systems and where possible promote the use of budget support that is implemented and reported upon by SIG.",""],[1,"77","13","Rationale Disclosure for Off-System Aid Delivery","If a development partner opts to use a delivery mechanism outside the country system, the Partner will detail the rationale and will indicate how it will work with the Government to better align its support in the future.",""],[1,"78","2","Development Partner Mission Coordination and Moratorium Compliance","Development Partners agree to ensure that their missions and program management and monitoring visits are carefully coordinated with the Government, seek at all times to meet the timing requirements of SIG and respect a decision by the SIG to place a moratorium on Missions during the period of budget preparations.",""],[1,"78","4","Information Collection and Sharing Mechanism Strengthening","SIG will strengthen its mechanisms for collecting and sharing information in an effort to maximize transparency and accountability for the benefit of all Solomon Islanders as well for development partners.",""],[1,"78","5","Development Assistance Information Collection and Verification System","SIG through MDPAC and the annual budget process will continue to collect development assistance information from ministries and all national stakeholders in an effort to improve coordination and availability of information.","MDPAC"],[1,"78","6","Regular Development Partner Consultation Mechanism","SIG undertakes to pursue regular consultations with all development partners to ensure a full understanding of its development priorities, while encouraging development partners to provide information on their longer-term intentions with respect to support.",""],[1,"78","7","Annual Development Partner Information Sharing and Multi-Year Agreement Mechanism","development partners will share annually information on their programs and where feasible conclude multi-year agreements with SIG to enhance the predictability of development assistance.",""],[1,"78","8","Annual Development Partner Reporting to MDPAC","Development partners will provide an annual report to MDPAC on their contribution to the NDS objectives and more specifically to the MTDP.","MDPAC"],[1,"78","9","Development Results Measurement and Management Instruments","SIG will develop instruments for measuring and managing development results, including the identification of performance indicators for the NDS and MTDP that can be incorporated in the recurrent and development budgets and the Aid Information and Management System.",""],[1,"78","10","Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Strengthening","SIG will strengthen monitoring and evaluation capacities, and development partners will support the implementation of a results-based delivery framework and accountability mechanism.",""],[1,"78","11","Joint Aid Effectiveness Review Mechanism","SIG and development partners will periodically conduct joint reviews on progress in realization of commitments on aid effectiveness and achievement of development results.",""],[1,"79","1","Stakeholder Participation in Development Planning and Implementation","SIG and development partners will support efforts to broaden participation of Parliamentarians, provincial and local government officials, civil society, private sector and media in discussions of country's development goals, the design and implementation of programs and projects and results.",""],[1,"79","3","Inclusive and Effective Partnership Framework","Promoting inclusive and effective partnerships with all relevant stakeholders towards the achievement of national development outcomes that includes a harmonized approach to crosscutting issues such as environment, gender equality, youth, climate change, culture and integration of disabled persons.",""],[1,"79","4","Cross-Sector Implementation and Development Partner Coordination Guidelines","guidelines have been developed to ensure a clear understanding of how SIG ministries and Government agencies will work together to strengthen cross-sector implementation and engagement policy with development partners",""],[1,"79","5","Multi-stakeholder Development Activity Design and Delivery Mechanism","SIG undertakes to include all relevant stakeholders, including NGOs, FBOs and the private sector in the design and delivery of activities for achievement of the national priorities as identified in the NDS and MTDF.",""],[1,"79","5","Government-NGO and FBO Engagement Framework Review","The mechanisms for Government/NGO and FBO engagement are currently under review.",""],[1,"79","6","Unified NGO Reporting Template Development","All relevant ministries of SIG, including MoFT and MDPAC, undertake to develop a unified reporting template for all non-government organizations to reduce the burden of reporting and promote a better sharing of information among all development partners.","MoFT | MDPAC"],[1,"79","7","Development Partner Coordination and Government-Led Aid Management","Development partners will be open and transparent in supporting initiatives of SIG and in working with other development partners, always ensuring that the Government leads these arrangements to maximize national ownership, efficiency and ensure partners with a comparative advantage are included.",""],[1,"79","8","Multi-sector Development Programme Coordination","Development partners in recognizing both the importance of a multi-sector approach to development and the coordination role of MDPAC, undertake to ensure that in designing programs and projects, resources are provided for the effective involvement of all relevant SIG stakeholders.","MDPAC"],[1,"79","9","Annual Development Coordination Target-Setting and Joint Review Mechanism","it is essential to set targets annually for both SIG and development partners to systematically ensure progress is made towards a strengthened development coordination agenda in the Solomon Islands.",""],[1,"80","1","Strengthening of the Stakeholder Forum","The Stakeholder Forum will be strengthened to ensure the full participation of all development partners and be an opportunity for specific consultations on the performance of the MTDP and the contribution made by development partners.",""],[1,"80","2","Annual Stakeholder Forum Progress Reporting and Target Setting","The Stakeholder Forum will receive an annual progress report on the implementation of the commitments under the Partnership Framework for Effective Development Cooperation.",""]],"19":[[1,"15","4","Staple Food Production Enhancement","While enhanced production of staple foods will remain a key element of the strategy and essential for food security and the well-being of the rural population (NDS objective two), a twin track strategy including the development of commercial agriculture and exports is key to growth.",""],[1,"15","4","Commercial Agriculture and Export Development Strategy","While enhanced production of staple foods will remain a key element of the strategy and essential for food security and the well-being of the rural population (NDS objective two), a twin track strategy including the development of commercial agriculture and exports is key to growth.",""],[1,"19","3","Sustainable Subsistence Farming Systems Promotion","Promote and enhance sustainable subsistence based farming systems including organic farming, indigenous crops and improved post-harvest handling to increase household food security and marketable surpluses and downstream processing.",""],[1,"19","4","Food and Livestock Policy and Regulatory Framework Reform","Promote, develop and reinforce the policy and regulatory framework for food and livestock production to better meet the changing needs of producers and consumers.",""],[1,"19","5","Agricultural Marketing and Land Use Planning for Rural Food Security","Develop agriculture and livestock through agricultural marketing and land use planning to improve food security, livelihoods and community sufficiency in rural areas;",""],[1,"19","5","Multi-disciplinary Agricultural Diversification and Agribusiness Promotion","use targeted multi- disciplinary interventions to diversify agriculture and promote agribusiness and alternative livelihoods.",""],[1,"31","2","Environmentally Sound Subsistence Farming Support","Promote development of environmentally sound and sustainable subsistence based farming systems, including organic farming, indigenous crops, and improved post-harvest handling, to increase household food security and marketable surpluses and downstream processing.",""],[1,"31","3","Agricultural Extension and Participatory Research Support","Strengthen agricultural support service for extension and research with a farming systems approach supported by active on-farm participatory research to help resolve day to day problems encountered by farmers.",""],[1,"31","10","Rural Local Crop Market Development Programme","Develop programmes for rural areas to encourage growing of local crops through the creation of local markets.",""],[1,"31","11","Agricultural Production Incentives and Development Subsidies","Consider incentives and possibly the reintroduction of initial \"development\" subsidies for expanding cash crop production and local agriculture food gardens to go into mass production.",""]],"20":[[1,"14","3","Disaster and Climate Risk Management Strategy","Medium Term Strategy 10: Improve disaster and climate risk management, including prevention, risk reduction, preparedness, response and recovery as well as adaptation as part of resilient development",""],[1,"43","2","Disaster and Climate Risk Management Strategy","Medium Term Strategy 10: Improve disaster and climate risk management including prevention, risk reduction, preparedness, response and recovery and adaptation as part of resilient development.",""],[1,"43","3","Strengthening Provincial Disaster Risk Management Arrangements","Nonetheless, the need to strengthen Provincial Disaster Risk Management arrangements has been recognised and support activities are increasing.",""],[1,"43","7","Disaster and Climate Risk Management Improvement","Improve disaster and climate risk management including prevention, risk reduction, preparedness, response and recovery and adaptation as part of resilient development.",""],[1,"43","10","Community Disaster and Climate Risk Awareness Raising","Increase awareness of disaster and climate risks at the community level by promoting risk awareness raising as part of ongoing development planning.",""],[1,"43","11","Disaster and Climate Risk Awareness Raising","Raise awareness of key development actors on disaster and climate risks, their causes and impacts (e.g. food production and security) to help raise awareness on potential management measures.",""],[1,"43","12","Community Risk Identification and Vulnerability Assessment in Development Planning","Promote risk identification and assessment including assessments of vulnerability and hazards as part of the community development planning process and ongoing identification of development needs.",""],[1,"43","13","Risk Information Management and GIS-Based Risk Mapping","Strengthen management, communication and use of risk information including widespread use of GIS and community \"risk maps\" to identify high risk areas and support risk informed development planning.",""],[1,"43","14","Climate Change and Pandemic Preparedness Capacity-Building","Ensure adequate capabilities to address climate change and pandemic diseases through increased awareness and implementation of strategies founded on research and development and information exchange.",""],[1,"43","16","National Climate Change Framework","Develop and implement a national framework for climate and",""],[1,"44","2","Routine Risk Management Integration in Public Sector Planning and Budgeting","Support routine integration of risk management into public sector development planning and budgeting",""],[1,"44","3","Development Planner Capacity-Building for Risk-Informed Planning","Build capacity of development planners at all levels to routinely integrate risk management (e.g. disaster risk reduction and climate change adaptation) into development plans and policies.",""],[1,"44","4","Risk Management Integration Capacity Building for Planners","Improve the capacity of sector and provincial planners to routinely integrate risk management into the project cycle including project site selection, design, implementation, monitoring, evaluation and budget allocations.",""],[1,"44","6","Risk-Informed Development Consent Processes","Support uptake of risk informed development consent processes to ensure risk informed site selection, design, construction and operation.",""],[1,"44","14","National Disaster Risk Management Plan Review and Update","Review, update and improve the National Disaster Risk Management Plan.",""],[1,"45","9","Climate Change Mainstreaming and Awareness Programme","Mainstream climate change by raising awareness and understanding of government and non-government policymakers and the general public about climate change and its causes and consequences and build consensus to facilitate, coordinate and implement climate change enabling activities.",""],[1,"45","10","Climate Change Mainstreaming Framework","Establish a framework for integrating climate change considerations into national development planning and relevant sectoral policies.",""],[1,"67","12","Climate Change Mainstreaming in National Policies and Planning","Integrate climate change measures into national policies, strategies and planning.",""],[1,"67","27","Climate Change Mainstreaming in National Policies and Planning","Integrate climate change measures into national policies, strategies and planning.",""]],"21":[[1,"11","7","Rural and Customary Land Availability for Development","Rural and customary land need to be made available for commercial and agricultural development.",""],[1,"12","4","Land Availability and Tenure Reform","Much land is under- utilised and the land tenure system is an obstacle to development.",""],[1,"12","4","Rural and Customary Land Release for Development","Rural and customary land need to be made available for commercial and agricultural development.",""],[1,"12","10","Land Reform and Land Development Programmes","Medium Term Strategy 4: Strengthen land reform and other programmes to encourage economic development in urban, rural and customary lands",""],[1,"15","2","Rural and Customary Land Release for Development","Rural and customary land need to be made available for commercial and agricultural development.",""],[1,"28","1","Review of Land Laws and Customary Land Boundary Delineation","Several laws need reviewing, with a first step including the enumeration and delineation of boundaries of custom and tribal land.",""],[1,"28","6","Customary Lands Recording and Registration Reform","Re-establish Customary Lands recording and registration process and ensure that the roles of chiefs and land ownership are recognized, respected, strengthen and supported.",""],[1,"28","7","Land Reform and Land Development Programmes","Strengthen land reform and other programmes to encourage economic development in urban, rural and customary lands.",""],[1,"28","9","Land Reform and Land Development Programmes","MTS 4: Strengthen land reform and other programmes to encourage economic development in urban, rural and customary lands",""],[1,"28","11","Customary Land Registration Awareness and Enumeration","Encourage and promote awareness on customary land registration and undertake enumeration of the registered customary land based on agreement.",""],[1,"28","12","Customary Land Rights Integration in Planning and Land Management","Reflect customary land rights in planning, law establishment and land management.",""],[1,"28","13","Land Registration and Tenure Rights Facilitation","Enable landowners to receive more benefits from development by encouraging and facilitating: (i) land registration; (ii) land rights and tenure system;(iii) protect interest of land owners.",""]],"22":[[1,"36","23","TB Case Detection and Treatment Improvement","Enhance healthy lives through improved TB case detection and treatment;",""],[1,"36","23","Leprosy Control and Stigma Reduction Initiative","reduce the spread, debilitating complications and stigma of leprosy",""],[1,"36","23","Food and Water-Borne Disease Outbreak Reduction","reduce number of outbreaks of food and water-borne diseases",""],[1,"36","23","Mosquito-Borne Disease Morbidity and Mortality Reduction","reduce mosquito borne disease related morbidity and mortality.",""],[1,"37","1","Market Regulation and Border Protection Measures","markets through the effective implementation of legislation, policies, MOUs, agreements and recognized standards such as border protection for public health threats and mitigation against harmful effects of environmental hazards.",""],[1,"38","7","Laboratory Capacity Strengthening for Health Threat Detection and Response","Increase capacity of laboratories to identify, monitor and respond to urgent and emerging health threats.",""],[1,"38","9","Health Threat Regulation and Surveillance","Increase collaboration and management of possible health threats through regulation and surveillance.",""],[1,"64","23","Health Risk Early Warning and Management Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of all countries, in particular developing countries, for early warning, risk reduction and management of national and global health risks.",""]],"23":[[1,"56","16","Physical Infrastructure and Utilities Upgrade Programme","Build and upgrade physical infrastructure and utilities with an emphasis on access to productive resources and markets, and to ensure all Solomon Islanders have access to essential services.",""],[1,"56","18","Safe and Accessible Transport Systems Expansion","By 2030, provide access to safe, affordable, accessible and sustainable transport systems for all, improving road safety, notably by expanding public transport, with special attention to the needs of those in vulnerable situations, women, children, persons with disabilities and older persons.",""],[1,"57","5","Quality, Reliable and Resilient Infrastructure Development","Develop quality, reliable, sustainable and resilient infrastructure including regional and trans-border infrastructure, to support economic development and human well-being, with a focus on affordable and equitable access for all.",""],[1,"57","10","Rural Roads, Bridges, and Wharves Rehabilitation","By 2020, at least 30% of Solomon Islanders in rural areas have access to essential services as a direct result of rehabilitated roads, bridges and wharves",""],[1,"57","12","Quality, Reliable, Sustainable and Resilient Infrastructure Development","Develop quality, reliable, sustainable and resilient infrastructure including regional and trans border infrastructure, to support economic development and human well-being, with a focus on affordable and equitable access for all.",""],[1,"57","13","Island Transport Infrastructure Improvement","Island provinces will have access to basic infrastructures such as better shipping services, improvement in airports and airstrips facilities to ease movement of people for economic and development activities.",""]],"24":[[1,"18","13","Financial Services and Credit Incentive Support for Private Sector Investors and Entrepreneurs","Facilitate, encourage and provide incentives to local and international financial institutions and credit unions to provide financial services and loans to private sector investors and entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"20","6","Expanded Access to Financial Services","Access to financial services needs to be improved with a broader range of financial services being made available.",""],[1,"21","13","Comprehensive Support Programmes for Small, Medium and Micro-Enterprise Entrepreneurs","Develop programmes to provide comprehensive support to entrepreneurs in the small, medium and micro-enterprise sectors, covering services in technical training, entrepreneurial training and business planning and access to financial services.",""],[1,"21","15","SME Development Policy and Incentive Package","Strengthen the environment for the development of small and medium enterprises including policies and incentive packages in targeted growth sectors.",""],[1,"21","16","Financial and Soft Loan Incentive Scheme","Facilitate and provide incentives to financial institutions, SOEs and credit unions to cater and provide financial and soft loans to",""],[1,"22","2","Rural Financial Services Expansion","Review viable options to improve access to rural financial services for savings and credit including options for: (i) mobile/telephone banking and micro-finance; (ii) rural people's bank to provide credit and financial services to local business; and (iii) special rural financing schemes.",""],[1,"22","2","Youth Entrepreneurship Investment Support","Provide support and foster an enabling environment for investment for young entrepreneurs to venture into potential identified industries.",""],[1,"54","17","Inclusive and Sustainable Industrialization Promotion","Promote inclusive and sustainable industrialization",""],[1,"54","19","SME Financial Services and Market Integration Support","Increase the access of small- scale industrial and other enterprises, in particular in developing countries, to financial services, including affordable credit, and their integration into value chains and markets.",""],[1,"54","25","Domestic Financial Institutions Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of domestic financial institutions to encourage and expand access to banking, insurance and financial services for all.",""],[1,"55","19","Private Sector Development and Investment Promotion Measures","Improve the environment for private sector development and increase investment opportunities for all Solomon Islanders.",""],[1,"55","21","Domestic Financial Institutions Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of domestic financial institutions to encourage and expand access to banking, insurance and financial services for all",""],[1,"56","10","SME Financial Access and Market Integration Support","Increase the access of small- scale industrial and other enterprises in particular in developing countries, to financial services including affordable credit, and their integration into value chains and markets.",""],[1,"56","12","Development-Oriented MSME Support Policy","Promote development-oriented policies that support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation and encourage the formalization and growth of micro-, small- and medium-sized enterprises, including through access to financial services.",""],[1,"69","28","Development-Oriented MSME Support Policy","Promote development-oriented policies that support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation, and encourage the formalization and growth of micro-, small- and medium-sized enterprises, including through access to financial services.",""]],"25":[[1,"47","1","Community Policing and Crime Prevention Model","Development of a community policing and crime prevention model is helping to reduce crime and family violence.",""],[1,"48","17","Quality Policing, Correctional and Fire Services","Promote a safe, secure and stable living environment by providing quality policing, correctional and fire services for all Solomon Islanders.",""],[1,"48","18","Community Policing and Correctional Services Strengthening","Strengthen the role of policing and correctional services, with close collaboration with the role of traditional leaders for community policing.",""],[1,"69","22","Institutional Capacity Building for Violence Prevention and Counterterrorism","Strengthen relevant national institutions, including through international cooperation, for building capacity at all levels, in particular in developing countries, to prevent violence and combat terrorism and crime.",""]],"26":[[1,"18","15","PPP Management Models for Sustainable Business Entities","Introduce PPP management models that could encourage and assist establishment of sustainable business entities.",""],[1,"21","8","Investment Policy and PPP Promotion Framework","Establish an investment policy that encourages private sector investment and encourages PPP agreements that will strengthen partnerships between private sector and the public sector and encourage development of Solomon Islands.",""],[1,"21","10","Public-Private Partnership Management Models for SOEs","Introduce PPP management models so that SOE's operate as financially sustainable business entities able to expand their service coverage.",""],[1,"21","11","Economic Growth Centre Development through Public-Private Partnerships","Review, assess and develop economic growth centres including industrial parks and rural growth centres through public-private sector partnership arrangements.",""]],"27":[[1,"12","3","Business Enabling Environment Reform","Policies and regulations that could be obstacles to growth need reviewing.",""],[1,"20","6","Private Sector Enabling Environment Reform","there is a need to improve the institutional and enabling environment for private sector growth including institutional infrastructure, policies and other legislation.",""],[1,"20","6","Transparent Legislative and Policy Framework","The transparency of the legislative and policy environment needs to be enhanced.",""],[1,"20","8","Commercial Law Reform Implementation","Government recognises that promotion of private sector development needs reduced costs of doing business and has initiated far-reaching reforms of laws governing commercial activity.",""],[1,"20","8","Predictable Regulatory Framework Development","More needs to be done to develop a predictable regulatory framework that protects the public interest and consumers while encouraging private sector development through increased certainty of business conditions and reduced transaction costs of doing business.",""],[1,"20","8","Weights and Measures and Quality Standards Enforcement","This includes establishment and enforcement of weights and measures regulations, and quality standards.",""],[1,"21","7","Private Sector-Led Growth and Investment Facilitation","Create a vibrant and robust economic environment to stimulate growth and investment through private sector-led growth, removing bottlenecks and other constraints to growth.",""],[1,"21","9","Business Tax Simplification Reform","Simplify taxes on business including customs, corporate taxes and elimination of exemptions to minimise the number of taxes, reduce collection costs, promote compliance, reduce business administrative and transaction costs and produce a level playing field and minimise opportunities for rent seeking.",""],[1,"21","12","One-Stop Shop for Business Registration","Develop a \"one-stop-shop\" where all requirements to set up businesses are available.",""]],"28":[[1,"20","4","Mineral and Hydrocarbon Resource Survey and Assessment Programme","Undertake surveys and assessments to identify mineral and hydro-carbon resources potential sites both in-shore and off- shore.",""],[1,"20","5","Improved Research Facilities for Investment Assessment","Encourage establishment of improved research facilities to foster rigorous assessment of resources and provide quality advice to decision makers and investors on the potential of investment.",""]],"29":[[1,"28","14","Customary Land Investment Facilitation Framework","Encourage investment from investors on customary land by facilitating proper identification and valuation of land type for industries, agriculture and mining to be sold or leased to investors, determination of financial shares, rewards or compensation to be paid for exploitation of resources on customary to landowners and agreements and MOU of partnership between landowners and investors and government.",""]],"30":[[1,"34","3","National Population Policy","National Population Policy - goal to improve harmonisation between population and development and an improved quality of life through more effective planning of development efforts.",""],[1,"34","4","Mainstream Population Dynamics into Development Planning","Mainstream national population dynamics into the government development planning process.",""],[1,"34","5","National Population Policy Implementation and Population Analysis Plan","Implement the national population policy, in particular identifying population patterns and trends and their implications for development, and provide a plan to address the areas in need of intervention.",""],[1,"34","6","National Statistics Programme Strengthening","Strengthen the national statistics programme and implementation of the new National Statistics Development Strategy.",""]],"31":[[1,"38","17","Integrated Tertiary and TVET Education System","Consolidate the establishment of a comprehensive, integrated system of Tertiary and TVET Education which provides quality education and relevant skills for employment, decent jobs and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"38","18","Adult Literacy and Lifelong Learning Expansion","Strengthen multi stakeholder approaches to extend adult literacy and gradually introduce lifelong learning approaches to education and training.",""],[1,"39","12","Second Chance and Re-entry Programmes","provision of second chance/re-entry programmes;",""],[1,"40","1","Lifelong Learning and Adult Literacy Programme","The education systems will gradually adopt institutional strategies and policies and adequately resourced programmes to ensure opportunities for all age groups including adults.",""],[1,"40","1","Skills Assessment and Labour-Market Responsive Curriculum Mechanism","To ensure the acquisition of new knowledge and skills, the Ministry will promote institutionalization of mechanisms and processes to assess the quality and quantity of the skills available and ensure that curricula and education and training systems are responsive to the needs of the labour market and society.",""],[1,"40","1","Cross-Sector Education and Skills Policy Coordination","Cross-sector approaches traversing education, science and technology, family, employment, industrial and economic development, migration and integration, citizenship, social welfare and public finance policies will be used.",""],[1,"40","13","National and International Scholarship Management System","A new system for managing national and international scholarships that provides equitable access, coherence with national education and labour market priorities and substantially increases the effectiveness of the results obtained is developed and implemented.",""],[1,"40","14","Institutional and Governance Reform for Technical and University Education","A new institutional and governance system is operative and capable of delivering quality and relevant technical and university education and developing solid partnerships with the private sector and the labour market.",""],[1,"41","21","Second Chance Education Pilot Interventions","Support pilot interventions for second chance education, in partnership with other DPs and regional initiatives.",""],[1,"42","4","TVET Expansion Model Development","Determine an affordable model for expanding quality and access of TVET.",""],[1,"42","5","Institutional and Governance Reform for Technical and University Education","Determine a new institutional and governance system that is capable of delivering quality and relevant technical and university education and developing solid partnerships with the private sector and the labour market.",""],[1,"42","6","Align TVET, Higher Education, and Scholarship Provision with Labor Market Demand","Match the provision of TVET/HE and scholarships with market demands and reduce over-expenditure of scholarships.",""],[1,"42","7","Labour Market Monitoring, Evaluation and Forecasting Information Systems","Develop appropriate information systems of monitoring, evaluation and prediction of trends in the labour market in collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"42","7","Public-Private Employer Partnerships for Demand-Driven Skills and Scholarships","Develop effective partnerships between private and public sector employers and SITEC to build a more demand-driven skills and scholarships development system.",""],[1,"65","19","Equal Access to Affordable Technical, Vocational and Tertiary Education","By 2030, ensure equal access for all women and men to affordable and quality technical, vocational and tertiary education, including university.",""]],"32":[[1,"43","15","Multi-Hazard Early Warning System Development","Establish an end-to-end Multi-Hazard Early Warning Systems for natural disasters including tropical cyclones and tsunamis.",""],[1,"44","7","Community Disaster and Climate Preparedness Support","Support community disaster and climate preparedness, protection and adaptation",""],[1,"44","8","Community Risk Management Plans and Safe Evacuation Centres","Support the development of community risk management plans in all high risk communities in the country and where appropriate, safe community evacuation centres catering for the needs of all vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"44","9","Community Response and Preparedness Training Programme","Train and organise leaders and key community members including representatives of vulnerable groups on community response and preparedness such as regular exercises and drills.",""],[1,"44","10","Climate Change and Disaster Hazard Project Identification and Resettlement Support","Use assessment data to identify specific projects that directly address climate change and disaster hazards such as resettlement of small island communities in collaboration with development partners.",""],[1,"44","12","Disaster Response Preparedness Strengthening","Strengthen preparedness for disaster response",""],[1,"44","13","Strengthening of the National Disaster Management Office Coordination Role","Strengthen and support the National Disaster Management Office (NDMO) to coordinate response including donor assistance.",""],[1,"44","15","NDRMP Implementation Support Arrangements","Establish operational arrangements to support implementation of the NDRMP including support for response preparedness (e.g. capacity, resource allocation, prepositioning of equipment).",""],[1,"44","16","Recovery and Reconstruction Preparedness and Coordination","Strengthen recovery and reconstruction preparedness and coordination",""],[1,"44","17","Recovery Coordination Committee Strengthening","Strengthen and support the Recovery Coordination Committee (RCC) led by MDPAC to coordinate disaster recovery and reconstruction including strengthening underlying recovery governance (e.g. capacities, financial allocations, roles and responsibilities).","MDPAC"],[1,"44","18","RCC Policy Development","Support the development of a RCC Policy to promote resilient and sustainable recovery.",""],[1,"44","19","Meteorological and Ocean Observation Network Upgrade and Expansion","Upgrade and expand meteorological and ocean observation network including a weather surveillance radar network.",""],[1,"66","22","Disaster Risk Management, Mitigation and Preparedness Improvement","Improve disaster risk management, mitigation and preparedness",""],[1,"66","24","Disaster Risk Management and Emergency Response Capacity Strengthening","Improved capacity in the Solomon Islands to effectively respond to and manage disaster risks and coordinate disaster emergency responses and rehabilitation.",""],[1,"66","26","National Emergency Operation Centre Upgrade","National Emergency Operation Centre upgraded.",""],[1,"66","26","Provincial Emergency Operation Centres Establishment","Emergency Operation Centres established in all provinces by 2018.",""]],"33":[[1,"55","10","Sustainable Tourism Policy Development and Implementation","By 2030, devise and implement policies to promote sustainable tourism that creates jobs and promotes local culture and products",""]],"35":[[1,"48","13","National Laws and Regulations Strengthening and Enforcement","Strengthen national laws and regulations with strict enforcement at all levels.",""],[1,"48","14","Law Reform Commission Support and Fundamental Reform Programmes","Strengthen and support the work of the Law Reform Commission and government fundamental reform programmes.",""],[1,"48","15","Justice Sector Leadership and Administrative Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the leadership, management and administrative capacity of the Justice Sector to deliver results.",""],[1,"48","16","National Judiciary Institutional Independence Reform","Establish the National Judiciary as an independent self- administering entity.",""],[1,"48","19","Judicial Capacity Building for Efficient Justice Services","Build the capacity of the courts and other legal offices for efficient and effective justice services in the Solomon Islands.",""],[1,"48","20","Law and Justice Human Resources Development Plan","Develop and implement a Law and Justice-wide Human Resources Development Plan to address the capacity building needs of all legal staff.",""],[1,"48","21","Courts and Judiciary Infrastructure Upgrade","Ensure the Courts and Judiciary has the necessary infrastructure to deliver core services.",""],[1,"48","22","Alternative Sentencing Options","Sentencing options which support alternatives to imprisonments such as parole, probation and community service, are used to better address the specific circumstances of each case.",""],[1,"60","18","Anti-Discrimination Legal and Policy Reform","Ensure equal opportunity and reduce inequalities of outcome, including by eliminating discriminatory laws, policies and practices and promoting appropriate legislation, policies and action in this regard.",""],[1,"63","10","Anti-Discrimination Legal and Policy Reform","Ensure equal opportunity and reduce inequalities of outcome, including by eliminating discriminatory laws, policies and practices and promoting appropriate legislation, policies and action in this regard.",""],[1,"70","13","Rule of Law and Equal Access to Justice Promotion","Promote the rule of law at the national and international levels and ensure equal access to justice for all.",""],[1,"71","17","Non-Discriminatory Laws and Policies for Sustainable Development","Promote and enforce non- discriminatory laws and policies for sustainable development.",""]],"36":[[1,"23","3","Strengthened Marine Safety Regulation Enforcement","There is a need for rigorous enforcement of regulations in the sector and current and new policies must address this issue.",""],[1,"23","3","Increased Penalties for Marine Safety Breaches","Penalties on service providers who breach safety regulations should be increased.",""],[1,"23","3","Marine Compliance Monitoring Capacity Strengthening","The capacity to enforce regulations and monitor compliance to marine and maritime regulations needs to be increased.",""],[1,"26","2","Road and Traffic Rules and Regulations Enforcement","Introduce and reinforce road and traffic rules and regulations through various law and transport enforcement agencies.",""],[1,"26","5","Traffic Act Enforcement for Vehicle Roadworthiness","Re-inforce Traffic Act 2009 to enforce vehicle road worthiness regulations.",""],[1,"26","6","Maritime Safety and Priority Area Identification Initiative","Create a safer maritime environment for the transport of people and goods and economic development through trade and tourism; identify priority maritime areas within Solomon Islands waters where there are significant, heightened and moderate risks to maritime transport.",""],[1,"26","7","Maritime Safety Information System Establishment","Establish a Maritime Safety Information (MSI) system within SIMSA.",""],[1,"26","8","Vessel Condition and Management Improvement Support","Encourage improvements in the condition and management of vessels through appropriate special funding, empowering SIMSA to more rigorously enforce regulations, and provision of training in small business management, planning and finance for shipping operators.",""],[1,"26","9","Navigational Aids Maintenance and Maritime Safety Awareness","Maintain navigational aids in good condition to international standards and promote awareness of safety requirements in all types of shipping including small boats.",""],[1,"26","10","Wharf and Anchorage Traffic Survey Programme","Conduct surveys to maintain current information on potential wharf and anchorage traffic as the basis of long term wharf construction and rehabilitation programmes.",""]],"37":[[1,"2","6","Public Sector Reform Programme","The NDS encompasses a public sector reform programme that will impart a clear sense of direction for our public service, improve accountability and enhance the efficiency of service delivery.",""],[1,"3","1","Strategic Partnership and Resource Mobilization for NDS Implementation","Partnerships will be crucial.",""],[1,"10","4","Whole-of-Government Coordination through Cluster Groupings","A \"whole of government\" approach is envisaged, with collective decision making through effective coordination by cluster groupings.",""],[1,"28","17","Communication and Cooperation Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen communications and actively encourage cooperation",""],[1,"46","2","Public Sector Reform Programme","A coordinated direction and harmonization at all levels through public sector reform programmes is a priority towards restoring professional standards and morale in the public sector.",""],[1,"46","2","Government Accountability and Public Service Effectiveness Reform","Strengthening government accountability, efficiency and effectiveness remains a key element for achieving stability and good governance at both the political and administrative levels.",""],[1,"46","2","Institutional Roles Harmonization Reform","A fundamental reform programme is needed to ensure the roles of public institutions at all levels are harmonized and enforced to support the quality of public service delivery to all Solomon Islanders.",""],[1,"47","6","Good Governance and Accountability Strengthening","Improve and enforce good governance values and practices and ensure accountability and transparency at all levels of governance, including strengthening the Service Commissions2 and Accountability Institutions3 to provide effective oversight and facilitation of government policies and programmes.",""],[1,"47","7","Public Service Restructuring and Reorganization","Review, restructure and reorganise the Public Service to ensure effective and efficient delivery of goods and services at all levels including rural communities.",""],[1,"47","8","Workforce Planning and Management Strengthening","Strengthen and reinforce systems for workforce planning and management, including the use of e-governance initiatives through the Human Resource Management Information System (HRMIS) Programme.",""],[1,"47","10","Performance Management Systems and Programmes","Establish effective performance management systems and programmes that enhances both staff and institutional performance and compliance to government policies and guidelines.",""],[1,"47","11","Public Officer and Stakeholder Capacity Development Programme","Promote the capacity development of all public officers and other stakeholders in both Honiara and Provinces to be equipped with relevant knowledge, skills and attitude to effectively perform their duties and responsibilities.",""],[1,"47","12","Human Resource Management Governance Framework Reform","Review and strengthen the Human Resource Management Governance Framework including the Public Service Act, rules, regulations, orders and other related laws.",""],[1,"47","13","Provincial Governance Strengthening Programme","Provincial Governance Strengthening Programme continues to support provincial governments for effective service delivery at provincial level.",""],[1,"69","25","Public Service Review, Restructuring and Reorganization","Review, restructure and reorganise the Public Service",""]],"38":[[1,"26","11","Airport Capacity Viability Assessment","Conduct assessment on viability of extended and new runway capacity, terminals and facilities of both provincial and international Airport.",""]],"39":[[1,"10","4","Investment Opportunity Promotion in Productive Sectors","The NDS seeks to grow the economy through creating investment opportunities in manufacturing and industry development such as tourism, agriculture, fisheries, forestry, energy and related sectors in an environmentally sustainable manner.",""],[1,"11","7","Economic Management and Reform Agenda","Improved economic management and reforms are needed that will ensure broad-based economic development and increase investment opportunities for all Solomon Islanders.",""],[1,"11","7","Private Sector-Led Growth Promotion","Private sector-led economic growth needs to be encouraged and facilitated.",""],[1,"15","2","Economic and Financial Management Reform","This requires improvements and reforms in economic and financial management and development of the private sector.",""],[1,"18","10","Financial and Economic Management Improvement","Improve financial and economic management through improved budgetary and planning policies and processes as well as forecasting.",""],[1,"18","11","Public Financial Management System Improvement","Improve accounting systems, financial rules and regulations to facilitate efficient and accountable delivery of public services.",""],[1,"18","12","Revenue Collection and Tax Reform Improvement","Improve revenue collection, financial management systems and the tax reform system to support private sector led economic growth.",""]],"40":[[1,"16","3","Export Crop Infrastructure and Standards Regulatory Support","Further development needs improved infrastructure in terms of wharves, shipping and marketing and a regulatory authority for food security and goods and services standards to meet the needs of domestic and international markets.",""],[1,"16","3","Large-Scale Plantation Production Expansion","There is a large potential to increase production and export from large-scale plantations such as the GPPOL oil palm plantation and out-growers, the RIPEL Yandina coconut plantation and Horokiki and other cocoa plantations.",""],[1,"16","3","Russell Islands Plantation Estate Repossession and Rehabilitation","The Russell Islands Plantation Estate needs repossessing and rehabilitation by SIG and traditional landowning groups.",""]],"41":[[1,"16","6","Regional Fisheries Monitoring and Conservation Measures","Through the Western and Central Pacific Fisheries Commission, Pacific Island countries have been effective in their push to establish a satellite vessel monitoring system, a regional observer programme for the tuna fishery and conservation and management measures for big-eye and yellow fin tuna.",""],[1,"19","6","Marine Resource Protection and Commercial Fishing Regulation Reform","Review and reinforce relevant laws and regulations to protect marine resources and to regulate commercial fishing in the boundary waters of Solomon Islands and international high seas.",""],[1,"19","7","Sustainable Fisheries Resource Management and Livelihood Promotion","Ensure fisheries resources management and promotion of livelihood opportunities are sustainable through the conservation and management of oceanic and coastal ecosystems.",""]],"42":[[1,"16","7","Tuna Loin Processing Investment Promotion","The Government encourages foreign investors to set up tuna loin processing.",""],[1,"17","1","Inshore Fisheries Development and Marine Resource Conservation","Development of in-shore fishery facilities including aquaculture, mariculture and other types of farming for subsistence and commercial development is needed for the benefit of coastal and atoll dwellers.",""],[1,"17","1","Marine Resource Conservation for Sustainable Harvesting","At the same time, the conservation of marine resources needs to be encouraged to ensure sustainable harvesting.",""],[1,"19","8","Fisheries and Marine Resources Development Programme","Develop fisheries and marine resources throughout the country through improved diversified products and improved marketing and information sharing.",""],[1,"19","9","Sustainable Fisheries Development and Resource Diversification","Use sustainable fisheries methods to improve food security, livelihoods and community sufficiency in rural areas; diversify resources in the inshore and offshore in partnership with resource owners and fishing communities.",""]],"43":[[1,"18","14","State-Owned Enterprise Governance and SOE Act Review","Improve performance, governance, oversight, financial sustainability and accountability of SOEs and review implementation of the SOE Act.",""],[1,"21","10","SOE Governance Strengthening Program","Improve performance, governance, oversight and accountability of SOEs and implement the SOE Act through the SOE Governance Strengthening Program.",""]],"44":[[1,"30","2","Poverty Alleviation and Food Security Measures","Increase efforts are needed directed at poverty alleviation, improved food security, increased diversification, food safety and nutrition.",""],[1,"30","9","Rural Poverty Alleviation Programmes Based on Natural Resources and Market Access","Develop and implement programmes to alleviate poverty based on natural resources and improved market access and a vibrant small holder sector in rural and remote areas.",""],[1,"30","10","National Poverty Alleviation Plan Development","Prepare a medium term National Poverty Alleviation Plan through stakeholder consultations in partnership with national and provincial authorities, civil society, NGOs and the donor community.",""],[1,"30","11","Rural Producer Support Programmes","Set up programmes that directly support rural producers such as rural livelihood government grants, loans and equity for small business start-ups and micro projects implemented by provinces and line ministries including direct dialogue between investors, resource owners and government agencies.",""],[1,"31","4","CEMA Legislative Review and Market Support Expansion","Strengthen and expand the role of CEMA through necessary legislation reviews to support marketing of rural agriculture products.",""]],"45":[[1,"22","7","Rural Roads, Bridges, and Wharves Rehabilitation and Construction","The NDS targets that by 2035, at least 40% of Solomon Islanders in rural areas should have access to essential services as a direct result of rehabilitation, and building of new roads, bridges and wharves.",""],[1,"22","8","Labour-Based Community Road Maintenance Programme","A new programme of labour-based community contracts is improving the condition of roads.",""],[1,"25","3","Rural Roads and Ports Infrastructure Improvement and Maintenance","Infrastructure - improve and maintain roads, feeder roads and other rural infrastructure and ports throughout Solomon Islands.",""],[1,"25","4","Road and Maritime Transport Services Improvement","Improve road and maritime transportation services including supporting the National Transport Plan and reviewing domestic shipping services.",""],[1,"25","15","Rural Infrastructure and Service Delivery Expansion","Facilitate infrastructure development for efficient, effective and quality service delivery to rural communities in water supply and sanitation, electricity, transport and communications - extending coverage of mobile telecommunications networks to all rural areas and facilitating affordable access by rural dwellers.",""],[1,"25","16","Provincial Service Delivery and Infrastructure Support","Improve service delivery by providing an enabling environment for provincial administrations to deliver goods and services and infrastructure development; strengthen their management capacity including in partnership with NGOs able to cost- effectively provide services on behalf of government within a transparent legal and regulatory framework.",""],[1,"25","17","Review of the National Transport Plan and MID Policies","Review the National Transport Plan and other MID policies to support implementation of transport related infrastructure.",""],[1,"25","18","Road Maintenance and Rehabilitation Programme","Ensure maintenance and rehabilitation of existing roads is effectively carried out; conduct studies on how to improve maintenance and upgrading of the existing road network including roads constructed by the private sector such as logging and mining roads.",""],[1,"25","19","Rural Road Network Expansion","Expand road networks to connect inland communities to coastal roads and maritime networks and to provide access to agricultural land and for rural communities.",""],[1,"25","20","Road Act Review and Renewal","Review and renew the Road Act to clearly allocate",""],[1,"26","3","Rural Transport Services and Safety Improvement","Facilitate private sector provision of rural transport services through improved infrastructure; improve safety of public transportation modalities such as bus services, inter-village pick- up transport, scheduled motorized canoe services and canoe based water-taxi services.",""],[1,"28","16","Rural Infrastructure and Service Delivery Expansion","Facilitate infrastructure development for an efficient, effective and quality service delivery to rural communities in water supply and sanitation, electricity, transport and communications and extending coverage of mobile telecommunications networks to all rural areas and facilitating affordable access by rural dwellers.",""],[1,"30","2","Rural Basic Infrastructure and Services Provision","Priority medium term activities include the need to address and meet basic needs of people in the rural areas such as provision of essential rural infrastructure and services (water, sanitation) and social and community development and improving the social well-being of all Solomon Islanders.",""],[1,"31","7","Road Access Improvement for Basic Service Access","Improve road access to facilitate travel and access to basic services, clinics, markets and other facilities.",""],[1,"31","12","Rural Road Access Development for Agricultural Areas","Build road access to interior areas with agriculture potential to enable population to access their own land for agriculture development.",""]],"46":[[1,"23","2","Inter-Island Shipping Scheme","The inter-island shipping scheme is an initiative funded by donors to service uneconomical routes.",""],[1,"23","4","Shipyard Infrastructure Development Programme","It is important that infrastructure development programmes focus on developing this in anticipation of future expansion of the industry.",""],[1,"23","4","Honiara Port Improvement and Expansion","the focus is on improving and extending the port in the current location.",""],[1,"23","4","New Wharf Construction","A new wharf is under construction (JICA funding) and about to be complete.",""],[1,"23","4","Port Storage and Access Road Upgrades","The port area will need further investment in increased storage areas and improvements to the access and internal roads.",""],[1,"23","4","Domestic Maritime Support Project Wharf Construction","A programme of new wharf construction has been ongoing with funding from ADB and NZ under the Domestic Maritime Support Project (DMSP).",""],[1,"23","4","Bina Harbour International Port Development","A proposal to develop an international port in Bina Harbour is becoming more tangible as reports suggest that land registration may soon be completed.",""],[1,"23","4","Bina Harbour Investor Identification Process","The next step will be to identify potential investors for the project.",""]],"47":[[1,"28","4","National Urbanisation Policy Development","develop a national urbanisation policy that supports urban and rural dwellers, informal settlements and return of unutilized alienated lands.",""],[1,"31","9","Constituency Housing Programme for Rural Dwellers","Continue with the constituency housing programme to all rural dwellers and ensure quality housing standards.",""]],"48":[[1,"31","13","Food Safety Laws and Regulations Reinforcement","Review and reinforce laws and regulations ensuring public safety in production and trade in processed food and beverages.",""]],"49":[[1,"31","14","Employment Opportunity Expansion and Rural Livelihood Improvement","Priority medium term activities include the need to (i) generate jobs and increase employment opportunities for the growing population across all Provinces including young people in rural areas; (ii) improve rural livelihoods and the wealth of all Solomon Islanders; and (iii) promote agricultural services to support small scale farmers.",""],[1,"31","15","Youth Engagement and Employment Programmes","Establishing programmes targeting young people, including young newly married couples, will help ensure they are engaged in worthwhile activities.",""],[1,"32","5","Rural Private Sector Growth Strategy","Develop strategies that directly provide increased employment opportunities through the encouragement of private sector growth in rural areas including fisheries and tourism.",""],[1,"32","6","Investment Programmes with Private Sector Participation","Implement investment programmes under SNIIP, NTF and other sectors that will involve private sector participation, leading to increased employment and improved living standards.",""],[1,"32","7","Farmer-to-Farmer Support and Market Access Assistance","Support farmers and rural communities through farmer-to-farmer networks; provide assistance in financial resources and access to inputs and markets.",""],[1,"32","8","Skills and Self-Employment Capacity Development","Ensure that people are equipped to respond to changing economic activities and skill requirements in the formal sector and possess the enterprise and business management skills to create self-employment opportunities in the informal sector.",""],[1,"32","11","Agricultural Rehabilitation Support Programme","Support and strengthen Ministry of Agriculture programmes for coconut, cocoa rehabilitation and other agriculture products.","Ministry of Agriculture"],[1,"32","12","Rural Training Centres Strengthening Programme","Improve and strengthen Rural Training Centres (RTCs) so that people acquire both life skills and livelihood skills to become self-reliant.",""],[1,"32","13","Small-Scale Local Investment Support","Encourage small scale investment opportunities by local people through Research and Development Centres, technical experts and skills support, down streaming processing and financial literacy so that people learn to save money with the financial institutions including women's saving clubs and credit schemes and other financial services.",""]],"50":[[1,"32","14","Labour Mobility and Overseas Employment Expansion","Increase labour mobility and employment opportunities outside the Solomon Islands",""],[1,"32","15","Labour Mobility Unit Strengthening and Labour Mobility Framework Reform","Strengthen the Labour Mobility Unit to facilitate increased mobility under the Recognised Seasonal Employer (RSE) Scheme and future labour mobility schemes and liaise with the Department of Labour to review legislation and design a broader framework for labour mobility.","Department of Labour"],[1,"32","16","Work Permit Process Review","Review work permit processes - types, usage and approval.",""],[1,"32","17","Minimum Wage Scheme Review and Enforcement","Review and enforce the minimum wage scheme.",""],[1,"32","18","National Labour Mobility Strategy","identify opportunities for labour mobility overseas, including but not limited to unskilled and semi-skilled jobs, in a broader range of sectors and with stakeholder consultations, formulate a National Labour Mobility Strategy including a policy to address local skill shortages.",""],[1,"32","19","Labour Migration Marketing and Management Mechanism","Maximise international opportunities for Solomon Islanders by increasing market share in accessible labour markets through development of mechanisms to market labour and manage labour migration and establish a National Strategic Direction for labour migration.",""]],"51":[[1,"33","12","Programmes to Encourage Men's Support for Women's Decision-Making Participation","Develop programmes that encourage men to facilitate the active participation of women in decision making, taking into consideration cultural norms.",""],[1,"33","16","Equal Opportunity and Participation Promotion","Encourage equal opportunity and participation in all decision making and work opportunities.",""],[1,"33","18","Strengthening Women's Local Institutions for Participation","Strengthen existing women's local institutions to make awareness and encourage Involvement of women in development decision making and implementation.",""],[1,"34","2","Target for Elected Women Leaders in Public Institutions","Establish a target for percentage of elected women leaders in MPs, Ministries, SOEs and in local government.",""],[1,"62","18","Women's Leadership and Equal Participation Promotion","Ensure women's full and effective participation and equal opportunities for leadership at all levels of decision-making in political, economic and public life.",""],[1,"63","4","Gender Equality Policy and Enforceable Legislation","policies and enforceable legislation for the promotion of gender equality and the empowerment of all women and girls at all levels.",""]],"52":[[1,"33","15","Gender-Based Violence Law and Regulation Implementation","Implement current laws and regulations in coordination with relevant public and private sector organizations, international bodies including family support, service providers, NGOs and survivors to address gender based violence.",""],[1,"33","23","Family Protection Act Implementation","Implement the Family Protection Act in coordination with RSIP, family support/service providers, NGOs, survivors and development partners.",""]],"53":[[1,"33","19","Gender- and Vulnerability-Responsive Water and Sanitation Programme Implementation","Ensure existing and new water and sanitation programmes are implemented based on accessibility by gender and vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"37","3","Hygiene Awareness and Behaviour Change Promotion","Improve hygiene awareness and promote behaviour change in communities' access to clean water and sanitation facilities in schools, clinics and public institutions.",""],[1,"58","4","RWASH Sanitation and Hygiene Access Plan","By 2030, ensure universal access to improve and equitable sanitation and hygiene for all, and end open defecation, paying special attention to the needs of women and girls and those in vulnerable situations.",""]],"54":[[1,"34","8","New Health Sector Strategy","The Ministry of Health and Medical Services is developing a new sector strategy.","Ministry of Health and Medical Services"],[1,"35","2","New Health Sector Policy","The proposed new health sector policy addresses these within four key groupings of objectives and strategies",""],[1,"35","11","Healthy Islands Cross-Sector Collaboration Framework","All should work together under the Healthy Islands framework.",""],[1,"35","11","Provincial Health Strategy Partnership Alignment","Provincial health strategies need strong partnerships with provincial government strategies to address health infrastructure and coordination of local government development efforts.",""],[1,"35","13","Health Workforce Planning and Redeployment Review","Health workforce planning will need to examine skills balance and possible redeployment from the main health centres to rural areas.",""],[1,"35","13","National Hospital Facilities and Referral System Review","Facilities at the proposed new NRH and provincial hospitals need review, together with the referral system between them to make the national system more effective.",""],[1,"35","13","Health System Governance Strengthening","Governance of the health system needs strengthening.",""],[1,"35","13","Health Financing Strategy Reform","Financial planning needs to rely less on donor support and more on local resources.",""],[1,"35","13","Health Resource Efficiency Strategy","Financial strategy has to focus on spending existing resources more effectively,",""],[1,"37","6","Partnership Coordination Unit Strengthening","Establish and strengthen Partnership Coordination Unit to harmonize development support to MHMS.",""],[1,"37","8","Intersectoral Health Determinants Coordination","Establish and improve linkages with other stakeholders in improving social determinants of health and health in all policies.",""],[1,"37","9","Inclusive Health Facility Planning Process","Strengthen processes and ensure inclusion of local and national government in partnership for all health facility planning.",""],[1,"37","10","Healthy Island Guidelines Framework for Development Partners","Ensure Healthy Island guidelines are used as the framework for development partners working at the national and community level.",""],[1,"37","11","Wise Heads Senior Public Figures Advisory and Monitoring Body","Establish a \"Wise Heads\" of senior public figures to assist in engaging effectively with other sectors and help monitor progress.",""],[1,"37","13","Local Health Development Planning and Monitoring Coordination","Engage through regular communication with the local authorities in planning and monitoring local health development activities.",""],[1,"37","15","Healthy Island, Healthy Schools, and Healthy Workplace Guidelines Development","Engage communities and their leaders, provincial governments with other relevant SIG departments, in the development of Healthy Island, Healthy Schools and Healthy Workplace's guidelines and indicators.",""],[1,"37","16","Healthy Life Status Criteria Development and Implementation","Provinces, AHC and AOPs to establish criteria for the achievement of Healthy Life status and include in activities and resources for implementation in collaboration between public health, local facility staff and other relevant partners.",""],[1,"37","17","Community Organization and Private Sector Engagement for Healthy Islands","Explore methods to recognise and include community organisations such as faith-based organisations and the private sector to address healthy islands.",""],[1,"37","18","Climate Change Mainstreaming in Collaborative Initiatives","Ensure the impacts of climate change are recognised and included in all collaborative initiatives.",""],[1,"37","23","Clinical Governance Committees Establishment","Establish clinical governance committees in main hospitals and health centres.",""],[1,"37","26","Health Care Partnership and Quality Improvement Initiative","Create partnerships among health care practitioners, patients and families and enhance the quality and safety of health care.",""],[1,"38","4","Medical Supply Procurement and Distribution Reform","Efficient, effective and accountable medical supply procurement and distribution services through improved financial resource management.",""],[1,"38","5","Health System Leadership, Governance, and ICT Decision-Support Improvement","Proactive identification, Improved leadership, use, governance and management at all levels of the health system and cost effective ICT solutions for delivering accurate and timely information for all health decision making.",""],[1,"38","11","Joint Outreach Planning for Universal Coverage","Develop joint plans and programmes at national and provincial levels for outreach activities to improve population coverage including identification of underserved populations and identification of bottle necks to universal coverage.",""]],"55":[[1,"36","7","Reproductive, Maternal, Neonatal, Child and Adolescent Health Strategy Plan Implementation","Implement Reproductive Maternal Neonatal Child Adolescent Health Strategy Plan.",""],[1,"36","9","Child Nutrition and Health Improvement Initiative","Improve children's nutritional and general health status through health facilities, schools, communities and regulatory bodies.",""],[1,"36","11","Certified Family Planning Training Course","Develop a certified family planning (FP) training course.",""],[1,"36","12","Family Planning Advocacy Campaign","Legislators, stakeholders, men and end-users know the availability of long-term methods, debunk myths of health concerns and advocate for their use advocacy campaign to make FP a national development agenda.",""],[1,"36","13","Health Facility and Community Linkage Strengthening","Strengthen linkage between health facility and community",""],[1,"36","13","Community-Based Maternal and Newborn Care Training Package Review","Review Community Based Maternal and Newborn Care (CBMNC) training package including FP.",""],[1,"36","14","Maternal Death Surveillance and Response Strengthening","Strengthen Maternal Death Surveillance and Response.",""],[1,"36","16","Adolescent Health Capacity Building and Youth-Friendly Spaces","Strengthen health workers', Peer Educators and teachers' competency on Adolescent Health issues and provide youth friendly space using a rights based approach.",""],[1,"36","18","National Preventive Health Promotion Programmes","Develop national preventive programmes for tobacco control, salt reduction, expansion of nutritional approach and encouragement of fruit and vegetable consumption and physical activity.",""],[1,"36","19","Package of Essential Non-Communicable Disease Interventions in Primary Care","Introduce the Package of Essential Non-Communicable Disease Interventions in Primary Care, including emphasis on combating diabetes within communities.",""],[1,"36","20","Evidence-Based Injury Prevention and Palliative Care Approach","Develop an evidence-based approach to prevention of injuries, palliative services for cancers, trauma and violence that have an impact on families and the community.",""],[1,"36","21","Community-Based Mental Health and Disability Services Expansion","Improve access and quality support for psychiatric and psychological services by the community including services for prisoners and private enterprises, eye care services to all level, preventative oral health care and disability services and interventions.",""],[1,"37","14","Healthy Families and Village Initiative","Strengthen Healthy Families and Village initiative",""],[1,"37","27","Health Literacy Support for Patients and Families","Support patients and family improve their health literacy, to navigate and utilise the health sector.",""],[1,"62","20","Universal Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights Access","Ensure universal access to sexual and reproductive health and reproductive rights as agreed in accordance with the Programme of Action of the International Conference on Population and Development and the Beijing Platform for Action.",""],[1,"64","18","Tobacco Control Convention Implementation Strengthening","Strengthen the implementation of the World Health Organization Framework Convention on Tobacco Control in all countries, as appropriate.",""],[1,"64","20","Vaccine and Medicine Research and Development Support","Support the research and development of vaccines and medicines for the communicable and non-communicable diseases that primarily affect developing countries, provide access to affordable essential medicines and vaccines, in accordance with the Doha Declaration on the TRIPS Agreement and Public Health, which affirms the right of developing countries to use to the full the provisions in the Agreement on Trade-Related Aspects of Intellectual Property Rights regarding flexibilities to protect public health, and, in particular, provide access to medicines for all.",""]],"56":[[1,"38","14","Early Childhood Development and Pre-Primary Education Access Expansion","Provide access to all girls and boys to quality early childhood development, care and pre-primary education by 2030 and to achieve full enrolment of all 5 year olds by 2020",""],[1,"40","4","Early Childhood Education Access Expansion in ECCE Centres","3 to 4-year-old children will be supported to expand access to early childhood education in ECCE centres.",""],[1,"40","6","Community Early Childhood Care and Education Centres","3 to 4-year-old children will receive improved quality early childhood education through community ECCE centres.",""],[1,"40","7","Quality Pre-Primary Education for Five-Year-Old Children","5-year-old children will receive quality pre-primary educations.",""],[1,"41","11","Early Childhood Access Expansion Policy","Develop new policy to expand early childhood access for 3-4- year-old in ECCE centres.",""],[1,"41","12","Pre-Primary Education Restructuring Plan","Develop plan to provide full access for 5 year olds by restructuring current Preparatory (Prep) into to pre-primary that mainstreams the use of vernacular language teaching.",""],[1,"41","13","ECCE Teaching and Learning Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of teaching and learning in ECCE.",""],[1,"41","14","Multi-Stakeholder Support for ECCE Centres","Promote multi-stakeholder approaches to increase participation and additional resources in organized learning in ECCE centres.",""],[1,"65","17","Early Childhood Development and Pre-Primary Education Access Expansion","By 2030, ensure that all girls and boys have access to quality early childhood development, care and pre- primary education so that they are ready for primary education.",""]],"57":[[1,"38","19","Education Resource Management Reform","Manage education resources in an efficient, effective and transparent manner.",""],[1,"39","5","Teacher Policy and Regulation Reform","providing teacher policies and regulations to ensure a sufficient number of qualified, professionally-trained and well-motivated teachers who are equitably and efficiently deployed across the whole education system;",""],[1,"39","7","Learning Outcomes Assessment System Improvement","improving systems and practices for assessment of learning outcomes in cognitive and non-cognitive domains and continually assessed as an integral part of the teaching and learning process.",""],[1,"39","8","Strengthening Education Policy Frameworks and Management Capacity","More work is needed to ensure stronger national legal and policy frameworks that lay the foundation and conditions for the delivery and sustainability of good quality education.","MEHRD"],[1,"39","9","Institutional Management and Administrative Systems Strengthening","Appropriate institutional management arrangements, governance and accountability mechanisms, management quality assurance, planning, information systems, financing procedures and mechanisms and general administrative systems will have to be developed.",""],[1,"39","9","ICT-Enabled Education Service Improvement","A better use of information and communication technologies (ICTs) will be harnessed to support evidence-based decision-making, strengthen education systems and provide education services more efficiently.",""],[1,"40","11","Senior Secondary Curriculum Reform","Key content reforms are developed and partially introduced to the curricula of Senior Secondary Education.",""],[1,"41","1","In-Service Teacher Training for Curriculum Delivery","In-Service Training - MEHRD develops more efficient and effective ways for upgrading the technical capacity of teachers to deliver improved curricular contents.","MEHRD"],[1,"41","2","Curriculum Cycle Management Reform","MEHRD develops more efficient and effective ways to design, deliver main curricular reforms and to monitor their implementation.","MEHRD"],[1,"41","4","School Management Capacity Development","School management's capacity is substantially developed to meet agreed and understood management performance standards and targets designed to improve school management and deliver NEAP education outcomes.",""],[1,"41","6","MEHRD Core Capacity Strengthening","MEHRD Management: strengthen MEHRD core capacity at the institutional, organisational and individual levels.","MEHRD"],[1,"41","27","Senior Secondary Teaching Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of Senior Secondary teaching.",""],[1,"41","28","Senior Secondary Curriculum Reform","Design new curriculum to ensure that senior secondary education will deliver appropriate knowledge and both work- related skills and transferable skills, including entrepreneurial and ICT skills",""],[1,"42","10","Curriculum Cycle Management Reform","Substantially improve the management of the curriculum cycle to accelerate the introduction of education quality improvement reforms.",""],[1,"42","11","Inspectorate Capacity and Role Strengthening for Curriculum Quality Assurance","Capacity and roles of the inspectorate are redefined and strengthened to allow their efficient participation in key parts of the quality assurance process regarding curriculum implementation and monitoring.",""],[1,"42","12","In-Service Training and Professional Development Improvement","Improve the quality and efficiency of the in-service training and professional development system.",""],[1,"42","13","National Teacher Qualifications Framework","Design a National Teacher Qualifications Framework (NTQF) to provide coherence and a reference to validate competences and qualifications provided by In-Service and Pre-Service training.",""],[1,"42","16","Core Education Management Capacity Strengthening","Ensure that core management capacities are strengthened -at MEHRD, Provincial and School levels- to provide the capacity to manage the strategic and administrative processes necessary to achieve the outcomes of the NEAP 2016- 2020","MEHRD"],[1,"42","17","Harmonised School and EA Management System","Determine a harmonised system to expand the quality of School and EA management to ensure the educational reforms achieve a real impact in the lives of the final beneficiaries.",""],[1,"42","19","ICT-Enabled Education Management Information Systems Development","Improve utilisation of ICT for management purposes and the development of robust and reliable MIS to support education management.",""],[1,"71","6","Education for Sustainable Development and Global Citizenship Curriculum","By 2030, ensure that all learners acquire the knowledge and skills needed to promote sustainable development, including, among others, through education for sustainable development and sustainable lifestyles, human rights, gender equality, promotion of a culture of peace and non-violence, global citizenship and appreciation of cultural diversity and of culture's contribution to sustainable development.",""]],"58":[[1,"41","3","Teaching Materials Procurement and Distribution Improvement","MEHRD develops more efficient and effective ways to procure and distribute books and other teaching materials to all provinces.","MEHRD"],[1,"42","14","Education Resource Procurement and Distribution System","Develop an efficient and harmonised system of education resource procurement, warehouse management and distribution of education resources to schools.",""],[1,"42","18","Education Resource Management Efficiency Reform","Make a more efficient and effective usage of the resources allocated to education - standards specifically address the general management of resources (financial, human and material) that are needed to develop a more efficient and effective system.",""],[1,"42","20","Coordinated Education Resource Management Approach","Develop coordinated approaches with communities, provincial governments and other key stakeholders to strengthen the efficient and effective use of the education resources.",""]],"59":[[1,"44","22","Holistic Natural Resources Management Approach","Promote a holistic, sustainable approach to natural resources management addressing forestry, marine resources and waste management.",""],[1,"44","23","Environmentally Sound Natural Resources Management Regulations","Promote development of environmentally sound and sustainable practices, principles and regulations for natural resources management to minimize environmental degradation and promote biodiversity conservation.",""],[1,"44","24","Environmental Degradation Awareness Campaigns","Sensitize the population on dangers of environmental degradation through awareness campaigns in urban and rural",""],[1,"45","5","Marine Resource Protection and Fisheries Regulation Reform","Protect marine resources, review and draft relevant laws and regulations concerning marine resources, regulate commercial fishing in the Inner Slot of Solomon Islands and consider reduction of deep sea fishing that destroys marine resources in relation to economic returns to the country.",""],[1,"45","6","Mining Regulation and Environmental Safeguards","Design regulations and enforce guiding principles on mining and other prospective mineral resources to avoid environmental degradation and potential soil erosion.",""],[1,"45","12","REDD+ Readiness and Carbon Financing Outreach","Conduct readiness activities for Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and forest Degradation and related conservation and sustainability measures (REDD+) and inform line ministries about the programme and carbon financing alternatives to logging, working with NGOs and CSOs on REDD+ compatible projects.","line ministries"],[1,"55","13","Sustainable Forest Management and Reforestation Programme","By 2020, promote the implementation of sustainable management of all types of forests, halt deforestation, restore degraded forests and increase afforestation and reforestation by [x] per cent globally",""],[1,"68","8","Sustainable Fisheries Regulation and Management Plans","By 2020, effectively regulate harvesting and end overfishing, illegal, unreported and unregulated fishing and destructive fishing practices and implement science- based management plans, in order to restore fish stocks in the shortest time feasible, at least to levels that can produce maximum sustainable yield as determined by their biological characteristics.",""],[1,"68","11","Terrestrial and Inland Freshwater Ecosystem Conservation and Restoration","By 2020, ensure the conservation, restoration and sustainable use of terrestrial and inland freshwater ecosystems and their services, in particular forests, wetlands, mountains and drylands, in line with obligations under international agreements.",""],[1,"68","13","Sustainable Forest Management and Reforestation Initiative","By 2020, promote the implementation of sustainable management of all types of forests, halt deforestation, restore degraded forests and substantially increase afforestation and reforestation globally.",""],[1,"68","16","Ecosystem and Biodiversity Mainstreaming in Planning and Accounts","By 2020, integrate ecosystem and biodiversity values into national and local planning, development processes, poverty reduction strategies and accounts.",""]],"60":[[1,"45","7","Climate Adaptation Resource Mobilization and Partner Coordination","Foster collaborative effort between all development partners to ensure collation of technical and financial resources to implement adaptation priorities.",""],[1,"67","4","Climate Change Education and Capacity-Building Programme","Improve education, awareness- raising and human and institutional capacity on climate change mitigation, adaptation, impact reduction and early warning.",""],[1,"67","16","Climate Change Education, Awareness, and Capacity-Building","Improve education, awareness- raising and human and institutional capacity on climate change mitigation, adaptation, impact reduction and early warning",""],[1,"67","19","Climate Change Planning and Management Capacity-Building Mechanisms","Promote mechanisms for raising capacity for effective climate change- related planning and management in least developed countries, including focusing on women, youth and local and marginalized communities.",""],[1,"67","29","Climate Change Education and Capacity-Building Initiative","Improve education, awareness- raising and human and institutional capacity on climate change mitigation, adaptation, impact reduction and early warning.",""],[1,"68","19","Climate Change Education, Awareness, and Capacity-Building","Improve education, awareness- raising and human and institutional capacity on climate change mitigation, adaptation, impact reduction and early warning",""]],"61":[[1,"67","25","Deep Decarbonisation Strategy","Availability and implementation of a transparent and detailed deep decarbonisation strategy, consistent with the 2ºC - or below - global carbon budget, and with GHG emission targets for 2020, 2030 and 2050.",""]],"62":[[1,"48","7","National Reconciliation and Peacebuilding Initiative","Focus on improving national unity, harmony and consciousness; pursue meaningful reconciliation between the people at all levels of the society based on the traditional norms of peaceful coexistence that will lead to national reconciliation and foster natural healing process as promoted in the National Peace Building Policy (NPP).",""],[1,"48","10","Support and Empower Community Leadership","Church, chiefs and community leaders to be supported and empowered.",""],[1,"70","32","National Peacebuilding Policy","Improve national unity and consciousness- National Peacebuilding Policy (NPP)",""]],"63":[[1,"48","23","International Cooperation and External Relations Strengthening","Strengthen and maintain traditional and emerging relations between SI and the international community to promote international cooperation.",""],[1,"48","24","Foreign and Diplomatic Relations Strengthening","Strengthen foreign and diplomatic relations that promote national sovereignty, political, economic, trade, social and cultural relations between Solomon Islands and the rest of the world.",""]],"64":[[1,"57","15","Rural Basic Needs and Infrastructure Provision","Address and meet basic needs of people in the rural areas, including provision of essential rural infrastructure and services (water, sanitation) and social and community development;",""],[1,"58","14","Land Reform and Land Development Support Programmes","Strengthen land reform and other programs to encourage economic development in urban, rural and customary lands.",""],[1,"59","18","Policy Frameworks for Poverty Eradication Investment","Create sound policy frameworks at the national, regional and international levels, based on pro- poor and gender-sensitive development strategies, to support accelerated investment in poverty eradication actions.",""],[1,"60","20","Fiscal, Wage, and Social Protection Policy Reform for Greater Equality","Adopt policies, especially fiscal, wage and social protection policies, and progressively achieve greater equality.",""],[1,"60","22","Rural Infrastructure and Agricultural Services Investment","Increase investment in rural infrastructure, agricultural research and extension services, technology development and plant and livestock",""],[1,"60","25","Drying, Storage and Processing Facilities Development","Access to drying, storage and processing facilities - to be developed",""],[1,"62","7","Rural Infrastructure and Agricultural Services Investment","2. Increase investment, in rural infrastructure, agricultural research and extension services, technology development and plant and livestock",""],[1,"62","10","Drying, Storage and Processing Facilities Development","Access to drying, storage and processing facilities - to be developed",""]],"65":[[1,"58","21","Affordable Housing and Slum Upgrading Programme","By 2030, ensure access for all to adequate, safe and affordable housing and basic services and upgrade slums.",""],[1,"62","4","Affordable Housing and Slum Upgrading Programme","By 2030, ensure access for all to adequate, safe and affordable housing and basic services and upgrade slums.",""]]}});